{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives","id":1238822,"title":"Third edition: Solars past lives","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-26T01:42:50-07:00","id":1238822,"title":"Third edition: Solars past lives","content":"Question! Does the core book talk about Solar reincarnation and past lives, or memories of the first age? I'm having a flick through and I haven't found much so far in any of the sections I'd have expected to talk about it.<br /> <br /> I'm familiar with how it works in previous editions, just wanted to know how / if this one tackles it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T02:24:18-07:00","id":1238824,"title":"","content":"No. The concept is barely mentioned in passing. However, it is detailed in Miracles of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Exaltation unbinds from the soul upon death, and the divine spark flows back to the Unconquored Sun ready for him to choose a replacement.<br /> <br /> The exaltation remains touched by the legacy of its previous bearers and <b>fragments </b>of memories manifest as strange dreams, inexplicable emotions or waking dreams when triggered by locations or such. Also, artefacts, manse defenses, sorcerous workings, or various spirits and such might recognise the inheritor as though the were the same person.<br /> <br /> Basically. The idea to allow your character to have excuses for being drawn to artefacts or manses, stunt picking up on clues, or to form unexpected connections or inexplicable enemities with spirits (see Tale of Visiting Flare), and such without characterisation being taken over by the passed life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-26-2018, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T02:27:41-07:00","id":1238825,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what Grey said. We're probably not going to be getting tons of it this time around due to the amount of focus it got last time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T02:51:17-07:00","id":1238827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1238824#post1238824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. The concept is barely mentioned in passing. However, it is detailed in Miracles of the Solar Exalted... <br /> <br /> *snip*<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect. Also I totally forgot about the Miracles book so I've ordered that, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":1079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","user":"Megapope","date":". 07-26-2018, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T02:54:16-07:00","id":1238828,"title":"","content":"MotES also added a touch more on the Lunar Bonds that might have formed. I anticipate that Lunars : Fangs at the Gate (FatG?) may have more to say about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:16:14-07:00","id":1238836,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Vance has said that in 3E the solar/lunar bond was a thing the exalted did after some sort of war between the two, as part of the peace treaty or something.<br /> <br /> It's connected to the exaltations of the pair and thus is always inherited by their reincarnations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:22:15-07:00","id":1238837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1238836#post1238836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Vance has said that in 3E the solar/lunar bond was a thing the exalted did after some sort of war between the two, as part of the peace treaty or something.<br /> <br /> It's connected to the exaltations of the pair and thus is always inherited by their reincarnations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooooooh I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:45:06-07:00","id":1238844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1238836#post1238836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Vance has said that in 3E the solar/lunar bond was a thing the exalted did after some sort of war between the two, as part of the peace treaty or something.<br /> <br /> It's connected to the exaltations of the pair and thus is always inherited by their reincarnations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait what? Are you positive on that? I'm not *against* the concept as it is, but I'm a little surprised they would set a First Age event in stone like that, considering how much history they try and leave things open to interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:53:33-07:00","id":1238848,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was on the discord.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming it's not gonna be any more detailed than &quot;they had a falling out, they made up, that's how lunar bonds came about&quot;. No indication of <i>when</i> it happened or how long it lasted or who started it or anything. It's gonna be about as concrete as the era names from Arms of the Chosen.<br /> <br /> Here, I found the post:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://78.media.tumblr.com/a03db99872bcdaec241456cfdcee1424/tumblr_pcgzpqgwXc1sateyko1_540.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 07-26-2018, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:59:09-07:00","id":1238850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1238848#post1238848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming it's not gonna be any more detailed than &quot;they had a falling out, they made up, that's how lunar bonds came about&quot;. No indication of <i>when</i> it happened or how long it lasted or who started it or anything. It's gonna be about as concrete as the era names from Arms of the Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So is it less &quot;all of them did it then&quot; and more &quot;this is how the tradition started&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T04:04:19-07:00","id":1238851,"title":"","content":"No, it was like a single, permanent thing they did. Probably a working or something. <br /> <br /> Later on Vance talks about the bond burying something the resurfaced after the Usurpation. Like, the Usurpation <i>changed</i> the lunars, and it was because it severed the solar bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T06:48:04-07:00","id":1238894,"title":"","content":"Well, that's a big piece of intel. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:13:46-07:00","id":1238917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1238836#post1238836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Vance has said that in 3E the solar/lunar bond was a thing the exalted did after some sort of war between the two, as part of the peace treaty or something.<br /> <br /> It's connected to the exaltations of the pair and thus is always inherited by their reincarnations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait I thought that Lunars were going to be able to choose who they bonded with. Now it's back to always having a destined match but now you can opt in instead of having it required? I'm not sure if I like that as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:29:23-07:00","id":1238922,"title":"","content":"Your past life chose. Now you're stuck with the owner of the exaltation they picked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:42:50-07:00","id":1238930,"title":"","content":"Considering how the impact of past lives is supposed to be so much lessened in this edition, I view this as a step backwards for the line<br /> <br /> Edit: Also the one-to forever pairing doesn't even make sense in this edition because we don't have fixed numbers of each exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T09:09:21-07:00","id":1238938,"title":"","content":"It's a thing the exalted did back in the first age. So the bond exists between however many solars there were active at the time and that many lunars. <br /> <br /> There are at least a hundred lunars with no solar mate, and there could be a couple of dozen solars with no lunar mate, if their exaltation wasn't active at the time. <br /> <br /> And as for the impact of past lives, inheriting stuff like manses and relationships with spirits and junk has always been fair game. Think of it like, I dunno, a king and the captain of their guard. The captain's position always goes to their kid, as does the king's, so you get this long chain of kings and guards stretching back, each inheriting the bond to the other from their predecessor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:19:08-07:00","id":1238994,"title":"","content":"In my experience, some Lunar players detest having Solar Mates, others (including myself, to some extent) like it. But the ones who like it don't want their character to choose generally; they enjoy plotlines like meeting this random Solar and finding they've got a bond. That's the drama.<br /> (They may want to choose as a player, of course)<br /> <br /> And since there's a hundred or so Lunars who don't have Solar Mates at all (possibly more), those Lunar players who don't like it can just... not have a Solar Mate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:03:41-07:00","id":1239082,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Some of this would seem to align more with my interests. That's the last that I'll say of it until such time as I see it in its proper and finalized context.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1238851#post1238851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Later on Vance talks about the bond burying something the resurfaced after the Usurpation. Like, the Usurpation <i>changed</i> the lunars, and it was because it severed the solar bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely that's old news?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:47:24-07:00","id":1239108,"title":"","content":"Well, ok, it always changed them. But now it kind of changed them back. <br /> <br /> Like, it sounds like the original forging of the bond kinda suppressed the lunar's rage somewhat, sort of &quot;taming&quot; them during the first age, for want of a better term.<br /> <br /> This may have even put a spanner in the works of the usurpation. They were expecting the lunars to react a certain way, based on their calmer, more civilised first age demeanour, but instead they unleashed this side of them that had been locked away for millennia and suddenly guerrilla warfare. <br /> <br /> And now the solars are back, but that rage isn't going back in it's cage so now the lunars are sort of stuck between their tamer, bonded first age selves and their more visceral, ragey post-usurpation selves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:51:38-07:00","id":1239111,"title":"","content":"Was it necessarily something that affected all the Solars and Lunars active in Creation at the time, or just the ones who agreed to the terms of the peace treaty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:53:16-07:00","id":1239112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239108#post1239108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But now it kind of changed them back.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that the idea that the sudden, dramatic loss of the Solar Exalted caused the Lunar Exalted to kind of lose their minds is right there in the Third Edition core book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T18:30:02-07:00","id":1239130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239111#post1239111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it necessarily something that affected all the Solars and Lunars active in Creation at the time, or just the ones who agreed to the terms of the peace treaty?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the details of it have been talked about in public yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T23:36:20-07:00","id":1239205,"title":"","content":"Yeah, i'm really hoping it won't be some story like &quot;The Bond was created during this specific event and was the only time ever when it could be forged.&quot; It's too much of a story hook to just lock it out of reach.<br /> <br /> Then again, considering how the team has been handling the First Age history with the lightest of touches, I'm also expecting a very modular view of the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T01:13:01-07:00","id":1239222,"title":"","content":"Quoth the Vance:<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book isn't gonna say &quot;NO, YOU CAN'T MESS WITH THE SOLAR BOND AT YOUR TABLE<br /> But it's not something I see getting discussed in canon<br /> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T13:11:54-07:00","id":1239416,"title":"","content":"Mhnnn I've changed my mind; I will talk about some things.<br /> <br /> The Lunars' bond to the Solars has been a few things over the Editions. I've still not yet read the First Edition book (I might actually see about getting around to that this weekend), but I understand that to have characterized that as a matter of how in the First Age, they would engage in ritualistic political marriages, that would tend to recur over incarnations, and had left a lot of Lunars in the Time of Tumult with very deep senses of connection to newly incarnated Solars.<br /> <br /> Second Edition upped this to an outright metaphysical connection, each Lunar Essence bonded to a Solar one at the time of its inception, with an attached mythology of the Unconquered Sun having demanded it to ensure the hierarchy in Exalted ranks (with it having a certain tricky twist from Luna). It came through mechanically in the idea that when a Lunar would meet their bond mate, they'd automatically form an unbreakable Intimacy (not necessarily a positive one), and there was an overall sense of partnership. It also came with a Background to build on that, which as I recall was basically just bonuses and penalties to Mental Defence Value as it related to one's Solar. Glories added a few Charms that had some variations in the concept, but that was the core.<br /> <br /> Now, speaking personally, I actually have a preference for the idea of <b>a</b> substantial metaphysical element to the Bond, an idea of something in the Lunar soul that reaches out to and connects with the Solar that they have associated with for ages. It appeared that a number of people, including some writers, found something to stir imagination in that as well (for better or worse); in particular was ideas that Holden used to posit, in which the natural state of the Lunar was a kind of raging storm that the Bond could help to ground and focus. I will admit to having had concerns when it felt like the new developers were going to downplay that side of it (even if I was ready to accept such gracefully).<br /> <br /> What we have here appears to be something that blends the framework from First Edition with the most readily salvaged elements of Second, in the context of the new direction of Lunars in Third. I wouldn't fret too much over the matter of a background being given to it, especially if that should be given no more detail than ancient myth. The key thing, I think, is that it would be myth that characterizes the metaphysical Bond as a thing that evolved organically from the agency of the Lunars and the development of their relationship with Solars. I should think that will be particularly helpful in redeeming the concept in many eyes and validating that it is something primarily to the benefit of Lunars; in the absence of that, I fear that some people would default to an assumption that it was something imposed upon Lunars by the gods, and that just... has too much baggage.<br /> <br /> In that light, the primary significance I see in the idea that it's something that they opt into is that it drops the notion of a Lunar instantaneously forming a connection simply from meeting a Solar, and instead that there's a part of their Essence that is always ready to resume the relationship, which will have certain benefits and incentives, but that part is still ultimately leashed to the will of the Lunar.<br /> <br /> (Unless it simply means &quot;you always have an option to play one of the quarter of Lunars that never had a mate&quot;)<br /> <br /> As for how it formed, I wouldn't expect a working to do that, as I think a general thoroughline is that Exaltation is a miracle beyond even their reach. I would instead suspect that it would be an application of the mutable nature of Lunar Essence. Same as changing the function of their Castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:34:21-07:00","id":1239457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239108#post1239108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, ok, it always changed them. But now it kind of changed them back.<br /> <br /> Like, it sounds like the original forging of the bond kinda suppressed the lunar's rage somewhat, sort of &quot;taming&quot; them during the first age, for want of a better term.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chilled? Mellowed out? Soothed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239108#post1239108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may have even put a spanner in the works of the usurpation. They were expecting the lunars to react a certain way, based on their calmer, more civilised first age demeanour, but instead they unleashed this side of them that had been locked away for millennia and suddenly guerrilla warfare.<br /> <br /> And now the solars are back, but that rage isn't going back in it's cage so now the lunars are sort of stuck between their tamer, bonded first age selves and their more visceral, ragey post-usurpation selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can be an interesting conundrum - specially when it comes to the Lunar trying to deal with memories, emotions and attachment coming from its older, gentler past self. Dealing with all that baggage from someone you literally don't know if you can or want to be anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-27-2018, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:57:29-07:00","id":1239465,"title":"","content":"Tbh, while it might be interesting, I have to say I'd rather the change in Lunars between the First and Second Age wasn't something connected to Solars, but rather something they did themselves. Possibly deliberately, though it doesn't have to be.<br /> <br /> I suppose &quot;going back to what they were before the Solars&quot; is okay, though it's still a bit Solar-orientated...<br /> <br /> Hmmm... if the Solars fought them in a war, and either won or drew (the Solars did end up in charge, so I guess not lost), and as part of peace negotiations had this bond to connect Solars and Lunars as family so they wouldn't fight anymore... some Lunars might see that as a pretty bad thing, which the Usurpation freed them of, and so be very cagey about the Solars returning. And not because &quot;the Solars made people weak and rely too much on them&quot; which came across as a bit civilisation-hating.<br /> On the other hand, I can see it reigniting arguments about the bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T16:37:28-07:00","id":1239474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239465#post1239465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose &quot;going back to what they were before the Solars&quot; is okay</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that part specifically may not be as simple as it's coming across in a second or third-hand account. I speculate that it's more a case that they're unfettered in a manner that they haven't been since the Primordial War, even if they rebuilt themselves into something best suited for fighting against the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... if the Solars fought them in a war, and either won or drew (the Solars did end up in charge, so I guess not lost), and as part of peace negotiations had this bond to connect Solars and Lunars as family so they wouldn't fight anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of-<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026.wait.<br /> <br /> Oh God, <b><i>Eragon</i></b>?! Roll it back, roll it back!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T16:51:24-07:00","id":1239476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239474#post1239474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that part specifically may not be as simple as it's coming across in a second or third-hand account. I speculate that it's more a case that they're unfettered in a manner that they haven't been since the Primordial War, even if they rebuilt themselves into something best suited for fighting against the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly. I have no particular problem with them having been different in the Primordial War, High First Age, and Second Age. I'm all in favour of Lunar self-transformation (as it was a significant theme of the Lunar I played before).<br /> <br /> I'm quite interested to see how they have changed actually, even though it's really just a historical detail.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:08:50-07:00","id":1239480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239476#post1239476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite interested to see how they have changed actually, even though it's really just a historical detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>With what little that I allowed myself to gather from the playtest references, I don't entirely discount it as including some things in their Charms, but I think it's primarily in things emerging from the mindset and function of their Castes, as expressed in Anima powers, Lunar XP, and description of how one ought to roleplay their Essence Fever.<br /> <br /> As for the nature of those Castes, the idea of socialites has often been brought up. I think some things such as their physically oriented Caste might have been derived more from Sacred Guardian Beast imagery.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I think that bonding to Solars might have constituted a refinement of an ongoing process; that even without them, after the War of the Gods they were adopting a new demeanour as guardians of the Realm that was more subdued. That's the other side to what the core said has damaged them; not just losing the Solars, but losing the Realm, and the lingering sense of connection to it owing to the Dragon Blooded erecting a new empire in its name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:40:30-07:00","id":1239495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239474#post1239474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reminded of-<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026.wait.<br /> <br /> Oh God, <b><i>Eragon</i></b>?! Roll it back, roll it back!</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT... The Inheritance Cycle was a great read! Unless of course you're talking about that movie. In which case, someone please erase that garbage from my mind!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:47:25-07:00","id":1239500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239495#post1239495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inheritance Cycle was a great read!</div> </div> </div> </div>It was so bad, you guys.<br /> <br /> Like, even the parts where Paolini decides to break with his otherwise-rigid adherence to the Hero With A Thousand Faces formula, it's still pretty bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-27-2018, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:02:40-07:00","id":1239506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239500#post1239500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was so bad, you guys.<br /> <br /> Like, even the parts where Paolini decides to break with his otherwise-rigid adherence to the Hero With A Thousand Faces formula, it's still pretty bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel bad derailing this thread further, but dear god the entire series was just him writing himself further into a corner and having no where to go or no ability to end it satisfyingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:20:07-07:00","id":1239509,"title":"","content":"Hey, remember how fans pointed out a minor grammatical fuckup in the first book, so instead of just fixing it, he canonized the mistake and made a point of turning it into this huge honking deal in the later books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:34:27-07:00","id":1239512,"title":"","content":"Darn it, there's got to be <i>some</i> other fantasy property in which a major but indecisive conflict is resolved by the sides engaging in a mystically bonded alliance or treaty...<br /> <br /> Or mythology... perhaps I should draw an analogy to the pact between the Aesir and the Vanir.<br /> <br /> Since the subject of Eragon has come up, I will grant it one thing; the scene in which the titular character (by that point in the story a virtual demigod) chases down a lone, young soldier, who was both conscripted and mystically enslaved (and when I say chases, I mean the manner in which a fox or a weasel might continuously cut off escape routes for a rodent that is trying to escape it), while the kid cries and screams and begs, and proceeds to strangle him to death without hesitation or remorse, is legitimately one of the most disturbing things that I've ever read, and if I was ever in the position to, I could probably call something back of the feelings I felt in reading that to try and capture some of the experience of some of the more... unrefined Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T19:55:21-07:00","id":1239534,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a> <br /> Boooo, and I'll say again, boooo! LoL, I suppose I can forgive you not liking the series. Different strokes and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239512#post1239512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the subject of Eragon has come up, I will grant it one thing; the scene in which the titular character (by that point in the story a virtual demigod) chases down a lone, young soldier, who was both conscripted and mystically enslaved (and when I say chases, I mean the manner in which a fox or a weasel might continuously cut off escape routes for a rodent that is trying to escape it), while the kid cries and screams and begs, and proceeds to strangle him to death without hesitation or remorse, is legitimately one of the most disturbing things that I've ever read, and if I was ever in the position to, I could probably call something back of the feelings I felt in reading that to try and capture some of the experience of some of the more... unrefined Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would point out, the soldier Eragon killed was not labeled a kid. The soldier referred to himself as to young to die, and had yet to marry and father a child. That does not make him a kid though, and the narration referred to him repeatedly as a man. Also, Eragon was many things, but remorseless is not one of them. Let me read the lines immediately following him killing the soldier:<br /> <br /> <i>Bile coated Eragon's tongue as he stared down at the man's slack face. &quot;Whenever we kill, we kill a part of ourselves&quot; he thought. Shaking with a combination of shock, pain, and self-loathing, he walked back to where the fight had begun.</i><br /> <br /> I don't believe remorseless is even remotely the correct word to describe him. Sorry for derailing the thread further, this will be my last post on the Inheritance Cycle series in this thread.<br /> <br /> Getting back on track, I actually use past memories to help nudge my players during my current game. They've been slowly recalling memories of a project they were involved in from before the Usurpation. I've kept the details very vague, but it's been a good tool to nudge them in a direction I wanted the story to take. Something I've considered is having them have a lucid, collective dream. I'd provide them each with a script, and let them read the lines of their former incarnations during a specific event in the past. This way they each might draw some differing perspectives of the event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T20:06:53-07:00","id":1239537,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">cleanbreakcleanbreak</span></span></span></div><br /> I do wonder if there would be an intention of past life memory and relationships to be more significant to the Lunars than other Celestial Exalted, or if the Solar Bond might be a thing that can stand largely on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T20:21:13-07:00","id":1239539,"title":"","content":"Spider hasn't had any distinct memories of his past lives yet, nor do I think him the type to let them define him, absent learning something absolutely huge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T20:40:37-07:00","id":1239542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1238824#post1238824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. The concept is barely mentioned in passing. However, it is detailed in Miracles of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Exaltation unbinds from the soul upon death, and the divine spark flows back to the Unconquored Sun ready for him to choose a replacement.<br /> <br /> The exaltation remains touched by the legacy of its previous bearers and <b>fragments </b>of memories manifest as strange dreams, inexplicable emotions or waking dreams when triggered by locations or such. Also, artefacts, manse defenses, sorcerous workings, or various spirits and such might recognise the inheritor as though the were the same person.<br /> <br /> Basically. The idea to allow your character to have excuses for being drawn to artefacts or manses, stunt picking up on clues, or to form unexpected connections or inexplicable enemities with spirits (see Tale of Visiting Flare), and such without characterisation being taken over by the passed life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really glad miracles isn't the core book because that's probably my least favorite mechanism of all time. I much prefer them as they used to be. Which is freeflowing into heroes as an automatic process. If the US has to choose than that makes no sense because the Primordials should have been able to tell him to stop picking people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T20:57:08-07:00","id":1239545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239542#post1239542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really glad miracles isn't the core book because that's probably my least favorite mechanism of all time. I much prefer them as they used to be. Which is freeflowing into heroes as an automatic process. If the US has to choose than that makes no sense because the Primordials should have been able to tell him to stop picking people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordials could not, and never could in any iteration of Exalted (including the one where that sidebar somehow made it to print), command the Incarnae to do anything. The Geas made it impossible for the gods to attack their makers, and that is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:00:44-07:00","id":1239547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239542#post1239542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the US has to choose than that makes no sense because the Primordials should have been able to tell him to stop picking people.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Primordials have that degree of control, then the divine rebellion makes no sense, because the Primordials should have either been able to say &quot;don't ever rebel against us&quot; or, once it was underway, command their invincible super gods to turn their violence upon the Exalted in their infancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:06:18-07:00","id":1239549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239547#post1239547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Primordials have that degree of control, then the divine rebellion makes no sense, because the Primordials should have either been able to say &quot;don't ever rebel against us&quot; or, once it was underway, command their invincible super gods to turn their violence upon the Exalted in their infancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I thought of it the wrong way. But if they just focused on him and killed him, he'd basically be unable to provide replacements for exaltations. half the deal was that the exalted would win regardless of what happened to their progenitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:12:49-07:00","id":1239551,"title":"","content":"I feel there's enough room for interpretation in the sentence 'directed by the Essence of the unconquered sun which carries his energic will' that it could be an automated process working under his guidelines if it matters to your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:14:42-07:00","id":1239552,"title":"","content":"Without going into too much detail, there was an idea behind the described process in which the unstoppable will of the Unconquered Sun is something that can survive in his Exaltations past the point of his theoretical and unlikely death; that he could continue to choose the Chosen even if everything else about him no longer existed.<br /> <br /> Whether or not that would be different is largely a thing to explore in games featuring the death of the Unconquered Sun, because it's not a question worth addressing in a setting premised on the idea that the Celestial Incarnae survived the war.<br /> <br /> It <i>might</i> be a question worth bringing up in the semi-canon additional Exalted that will be featured in the appendix of Exigents, but I know that new Exalted are a four letter word to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:16:24-07:00","id":1239553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239549#post1239549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose I thought of it the wrong way. But if they just focused on him and killed him, he'd basically be unable to provide replacements for exaltations. half the deal was that the exalted would win regardless of what happened to their progenitor.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming they could kill TUCS. While the Geas prevented the gods from attacking them, I doubt it would prevent them from defending themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T22:08:20-07:00","id":1239564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239553#post1239553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're assuming they could kill TUCS. While the Geas prevented the gods from attacking them, I doubt it would prevent them from defending themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. A lot, actually, nearly all of the &quot;Exaltations are automoatans&quot; things come from folks attributing to the creators powers and effects beyond what was stated.<br /> <br /> The Geas, as presented in its original form, prevented the gods from attacking their creators. Nothing said in it that they ahd to obey them, nor that htey couldn't defend htemsleves. Just that they couldn't directly initiate hostiliteis, which led to them creating the Exalted as the mistletoe solution. And once the war was going, one might think that the creators probably <i>did</i> just consider killing him, but well, Exalted, he's a badass, and even if they tried, it obviously failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:00:05-07:00","id":1239567,"title":"","content":"Thinking about the bond being created as an attempt to bring lasting peace I got to thinking: If the bond soothed the rage of the Lunars in some way, what did it do to the Solars? Did the bond actually amplify and accelerate the Solar's Great Curse?<br /> <br /> Probably not.<br /> <br /> Then again, I suppose it could have had a stabilizing effect on the Solars as well. Though this may have simply slowed the decent into horrible madness and corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:28:54-07:00","id":1239588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239512#post1239512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darn it, there's got to be <i>some</i> other fantasy property in which a major but indecisive conflict is resolved by the sides engaging in a mystically bonded alliance or treaty...<br /> <br /> Or mythology... perhaps I should draw an analogy to the pact between the Aesir and the Vanir.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thomas Covenant's &quot;the Land&quot; might be a better point of comparison. <br /> <br /> In the series, after High Lord Kevin utterly blights the land in an attempt to destroy the Big Bad (thus leading him to be called Kevin Landwaster), he establishes caches of magical knowledge, the Wards, hiding them and leaving clues to the next in each one. Only the First Ward is easily recovered.<br /> <br /> When humanity returns to the Land, they swear a great Oath of Peace to prevent such a thing from happening again, and it has an actual psychological and magical change on the inhabitants. Among other things, ill health, even subtle ailments, are as visible as if someone had had paint thrown on them, and everyone is naturally inclined to pacifism.<br /> <br /> The downside is, they are ALSO utterly unable to make sense of more than the very basics of the First Ward, because their mindset is so utterly different from that of Kevin's people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T01:59:42-07:00","id":1239605,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this has also come up on the discord. When they say the gods &quot;choose&quot; people it's not a <i>conscious </i>choice. It's been compared to falling in love. The god decides you are worthy and boom.<br /> <br /> So even if they were told not to (because, yeah, the geas doesn't compel obedience but that's hardly the only option the primordials had) they'd still continue choosing chosen because they <i>can't help it</i>.<br /> <br /> Conky can't look at someone and go &quot;oh, I'd like to exalt that person but I cant/shouldn't&quot;. It's too late. They're already glowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T03:37:48-07:00","id":1239619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239567#post1239567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the bond soothed the rage of the Lunars in some way, what did it do to the Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an overall preference for the Bond being exclusively a property of the Lunar Exalted, so my perspective on what they got out of it would be a positive, even perhaps somewhat devotional, relationship from the Lunars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br 