d by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239639#post1239639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I just think if the US was in charge of the exaltation process we wouldn't have gotten half the solars we currently have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T05:56:09-07:00","id":1239645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239644#post1239644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such as...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Havesh and Arianna off the top of my head. They're pretty much psychopaths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:06:22-07:00","id":1239648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239645#post1239645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havesh and Arianna off the top of my head. They're pretty much psychopaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, no, they're not. <br /> <br /> Second, even assuming you're just using the term informally, myth in general has quite a tradition of the gods choosing (or fathering) unstable, violence-prone champions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:11:26-07:00","id":1239652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239639#post1239639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll probably see what things exigents have</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you've been a bit out of the loop, I think some extra details are needed:<br /> <br /> Three of the new Exalted types, those featured in that little teaser art in the core, are the Umbral exalted, the Dream-Souled, and the Hearteaters. Robert and Eric have decided to integrate them be making them canon optional; they'll get details and backstories, but not be heavily integrated into the setting. Hence, they'll be featured in the Appendix of Exigents.<br /> <br /> The significance of my comment about Incarnae is the fact that part of how the developers have defined Exaltation is as something that requires a patron of around the same power as the Incarnae, and it may be that part of the backstories of some of those new Exalted is that something bad happening to their patron messed them up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">can't change that</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> You never know.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239645#post1239645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Havesh and Arianna off the top of my head. They're pretty much psychopaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Havesh gets vastly exaggerated in internet discussions from how he was actually portrayed in the Caste Book.<br /> <br /> You're straight up incorrect about Arianna. Name one objectionable thing that she's ever done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:30:15-07:00","id":1239657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239648#post1239648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, no, they're not.<br /> <br /> Second, even assuming you're just using the term informally, myth in general has quite a tradition of the gods choosing (or fathering) unstable, violence-prone champions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I know solars were originally supposed to be classical heroes but the books don't treat them as such. They treat them as perfect and righteous beings who are inflicted with something external. Which is a big problem with the GC for me. It basically means it wasn't them who were flawed and mad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I actually know about those. I recently caught up with most things. I didn't know they were in the exigent book. Also, part of the reason I will always dislike exigents is because I really want sidereals and that's like at least 2 years off because of them. <br /> <br /> Also, it's been a while so I could be confusing her with someone else. I'll have to reread the old solar npcs. I do remember there being more than a few questionable solars. I have no problem with questionable solars. In fact, I more than encourage it but 1 and 2e books have had a habit of portraying questionable actions as good. Which I do have an issue with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-28-2018, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:38:01-07:00","id":1239660,"title":"","content":"Hmm, beginnings of a Great Curse argument.<br /> <img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/NUfmWRCAdzyy4/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:45:57-07:00","id":1239662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239657#post1239657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[the books] treat [Solars] as perfect and righteous beings who are inflicted with something external.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect? No. Not even a little. The books went out of their way to literally (and I do mean &quot;literally,&quot; not figuratively) demonstrate how <b>perfection doesn't actually exist.</b><br /> <br /> Righteous, on the other hand, sure, some of them, but <i>righteousness is not incompatible with instability or violence</i>. In fact those very things often go hand-in-hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-28-2018, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T07:37:33-07:00","id":1239674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239657#post1239657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, it's been a while so I could be confusing her with someone else. I'll have to reread the old solar npcs. I do remember there being more than a few questionable solars. I have no problem with questionable solars. In fact, I more than encourage it but 1 and 2e books have had a habit of portraying questionable actions as good. Which I do have an issue with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably thinking of Lyta.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T08:00:48-07:00","id":1239685,"title":"","content":"Even Lyta is politically motivated, and has an upbringing that would desensitize her to the lives of people that she views as enemies.<br /> <br /> If that makes her a psychopath, than a sizable proportion if not majority of people throughout history have been psychopaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T08:14:28-07:00","id":1239690,"title":"","content":"Oh, I certainly agree that their actions make some sense in terms of their situation, and don't need to be explained by the socially problematic effects of being a psychopath.<br /> <br /> They are bad people though.*<br /> Personally, I have no objection to the Unconquered Sun exalting bad people. If PCs feel that he should choose more virtuous people, they can bring it up with him. Possibly violently.<br /> <br /> *I was thinking about Lyra and her mirrors... And it occurred to me that Obsidian Butterfly, the Solar in our game who wants to cut people's hearts as a sacrifice to the Unconquered Sun, is otherwise one of the more moral members of the group. That probably says more about the rest of us than her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-28-2018, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T14:56:45-07:00","id":1239804,"title":"","content":"I always see people bring her up, but does Lyta particularly stand out in the concept of &quot;bad&quot; as opposed to most of the rest of the setting?<br /> <br /> It seems like her biggest sin is killing the Realm's Wyld Hunt Dragon Blooded she captures in battle, but at the same time she and every other Solar are likely to receive the exact same treatment if they were the losers defeated by a Wyld Hunt of Dragon Blooded. So I don't know if she comes off as all that more ruthless than a lot of other individuals in the setting, many player characters included.<br /> <br /> At worst it seems like she treats the Realm's Dragon Blooded pretty similar to the same way they treat her or other Solar Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-28-2018, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T17:22:42-07:00","id":1239848,"title":"","content":"I suspect that Lyta came across as bad to the people that first read her due to her professed desire to ritualistically execute her enemies, which... has been fairly standard throughout human history, but I'd say that a lot of fiction up to that point would have been more likely to attribute to villains.<br /> <br /> Mind, if I had been there at the time, I imagine that I would have been saying such right alongside everybody else, for a couple of reasons. But my current world view is one in which I don't really see any value or sense in condemning ancient world politics and morality, nor do I see the purpose of fiction depicting such to be reinforcing the rightness of contemporary views by having a representative of them righteously opposed to things as they actually are.<br /> <br /> (I don't exactly apply that lens to matters of rights and representations for traditionally marginalized people, for reasons of deconstructing the sense that such marginalization is the naturally encoded default)<br /> <br /> Besides which, it helps that Lyta's ire is directed towards the corrupt and powerful in her world view, rather than punching down. Really, the same goes with Havesh (including the point that I'm really convinced that there's a not particularly subtle subtext in his story that he kind of hovers on the verge of convincing himself to be a champion and emancipator for the oppressed underclass from which he originates).<br /> <br /> As for the significance of being Chosen by the Unconquered Sun, I would frame it in terms of him being compelled by people that are passionately motivated, and if not particularly good, then at least not heavily inclined towards utilising their power to contribute to the suffering and exploitation of the already oppressed.<br /> <br /> In that regard, one could read Arianna as being something like among the worst of them, as her attitude towards most people as I recall it was somewhat cold and elitist, but not necessarily in a manner that is going to make life worse for the majority of people.<br /> <br /> They might not be exactly nice, but people have often found cathartic value in stories of heroes who were not particularly nice to those perceived to be the source of their woes, and practical value in using such people in capacities such as revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T19:23:45-07:00","id":1239873,"title":"","content":"Since the subject of whether or not Lunars can form mystical bonds that endure over lifetimes at will to anybody has come up elsewhere:<br /> <br /> My read on the situation is that it's not exactly a property of Lunar Exaltation that they can just harness as they please, and that it's more like remaking their Castes; that it requires drastic, dramatic circumstances, something that collectively resonates through many if not most if not all of them, and to have a certain foundation in their underlying mythology.<br /> <br /> I think that it's supposed to be something that worked because political marriage to end a harmful conflict with what were not only fellow Exalted, but the Chosen of the Sun, who possesses a dualistic relationship with their Moon, as well as being heroes mighty enough to temper and focus them in their own right, is something that had a powerful enough weight to leave a lasting impression upon their Essence.<br /> <br /> One thing that I suspect <i>will</i> be ambiguous is exactly how many Lunars and Solars got that deal; it can't be more than three quarters of the former, and I suspect that there will be room for their to be fewer even than that, that there are Solar Essences for which there is no waiting Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T22:26:14-07:00","id":1239905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239848#post1239848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that Lyta came across as bad to the people that first read her due to her professed desire to ritualistically execute her enemies, which... has been fairly standard throughout human history, but I'd say that a lot of fiction up to that point would have been more likely to attribute to villains.<br /> <br /> Mind, if I had been there at the time, I imagine that I would have been saying such right alongside everybody else, for a couple of reasons. But my current world view is one in which I don't really see any value or sense in condemning ancient world politics and morality, nor do I see the purpose of fiction depicting such to be reinforcing the rightness of contemporary views by having a representative of them righteously opposed to things as they actually are.<br /> <br /> (I don't exactly apply that lens to matters of rights and representations for traditionally marginalized people, for reasons of deconstructing the sense that such marginalization is the naturally encoded default)<br /> <br /> Besides which, it helps that Lyta's ire is directed towards the corrupt and powerful in her world view, rather than punching down. Really, the same goes with Havesh (including the point that I'm really convinced that there's a not particularly subtle subtext in his story that he kind of hovers on the verge of convincing himself to be a champion and emancipator for the oppressed underclass from which he originates).<br /> <br /> As for the significance of being Chosen by the Unconquered Sun, I would frame it in terms of him being compelled by people that are passionately motivated, and if not particularly good, then at least not heavily inclined towards utilising their power to contribute to the suffering and exploitation of the already oppressed.<br /> <br /> In that regard, one could read Arianna as being something like among the worst of them, as her attitude towards most people as I recall it was somewhat cold and elitist, but not necessarily in a manner that is going to make life worse for the majority of people.<br /> <br /> They might not be exactly nice, but people have often found cathartic value in stories of heroes who were not particularly nice to those perceived to be the source of their woes, and practical value in using such people in capacities such as revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lyta has two things going on that I think get mixed-up.<br /> <br /> 1) Castebook: Dawn pretty much states, outright and OOC, if I remember right, is a lot of her issues are less that she's like, soem inherently bad person and more that <i>she's 18</i>. I remember back in the day that this was probably more her issue. She was a teenager who was being manipulated and who was probably more than the Gold Faction handlers could control. Teenagers are edgelordy little shits given the options and wil fantisize of all sorts of crazy shit if given the opportunity.<br /> <br /> 2) Later 1e books and 2e in general more or elss mad eher mirror sacrofice hting canonical, which is to me an example of Flanderization more than it is something of th sun giving power to someone who probably couldn't handle it.<br /> <br /> Her and Havesh also to me are examples of people who the Sun liked as having <i>potential</i>. And ultiamtely, failed to realize it. Which is a pretty different situation than just people inherently evil and the Sun somehow in his (unstated) omnisicience should have sene better. To me, he just is fallable, which is something folks see to miss in discussions of the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T00:18:03-07:00","id":1239919,"title":"","content":"I disagree that the two are somehow squandering their heroic potential; one is building an army to take on the Realm, and the other is dismantling the oppressive caste system of his homeland by murdering and impersonating the elites. It's not like either is sitting on their ass binge-watching endless Netflix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T00:44:06-07:00","id":1239924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239919#post1239919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that the two are somehow squandering their heroic potential; one is building an army to take on the Realm, and the other is dismantling the oppressive caste system of his homeland by murdering and impersonating the elites. It's not like either is sitting on their ass binge-watching endless Netflix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. They're not virtuous and righteous, but they are getting stuff done. It's arguable whether it's good (and, honestly, while Havesh may murder people, the Bull of the North has probably killed far, far more innocent people than Havesh has in his imperial war of conquest), but they are the sort of people you might choose to recruit in a war against the god-worlds who made the universe.<br /> <br /> I think the reason people bring them up with the Unconquered Sun choosing Solars is because of the logic chain:<br /> The Unconquered Sun is good;<br /> So he'd choose good people;<br /> He chooses bad people;<br /> This makes no sense.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the problem is him choosing people, I think the problem is assuming he's good, from the perspective of a 21st century player. He's Zeus/Ra/Jupiter/Huetzilopochtli. Sure, he's better than the Titans, but he's not perfect. So sometimes he chooses people who seem to others like villains.*<br /> (And Luna... is insane. And the Maidens are inscrutable and weird.)<br /> <br /> *Lyta literally was the villain for our Dragonblood game, but then, we were Dynasts, so maybe we were the villains. And I used Havesh as King of the Casteless in Varang, someone the PCs cooperated with as his revolution distracted the authorities from the PCs plans to rescue all Djala slaves, and later killed because he was also cooperating with people that Sidereals+Kes had manipulated them into fighting. Well, actually they killed him because he was a suspicious foreigner in their enemy's palace who was trying to leave and wouldn't answer their questions. That's PCs for you.<br /> <br /> Saying this, I was totally fine with the 2e thing of the Exaltations choosing people themselves, and I preferred that to the UCS choosing them. But I don't think it's a big problem.<br /> (As long as there's some mechanism for the Exaltations to keep choosing people after the UCS dies, of course, otherwise I'd have had to stop people making new Solar characters in my game. Or Lunar characters.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-29-2018, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:18:57-07:00","id":1239931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239905#post1239905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her and Havesh also to me are examples of people who the Sun liked as having <i>potential</i>. And ultiamtely, failed to realize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that Havesh is truly wasting his potential. Why, in the single, solitary year that he's been Exalted, he's only managed to strike such fear into the hearts of the oppressive upper class of his native major city state that he's been dubbed with a terrifying moniker. Most Solars in that time have already unzipped and worn their first Ebon Dragon as a coat, as I understand it.<br /> <br /> Never mind any of that stuff I said about how he seems to be gradually talking himself into being a champion for his fellow casteless; if you don't come to that conclusion immediately upon being given greater power and opportunity than you ever could have dreamed of in your previously extremely underprivileged life, you've missed your window for your entire, several millenia long lifespan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:31:42-07:00","id":1239936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239931#post1239931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that Havesh is truly wasting his potential. Why, in the single, solitary year that he's been Exalted, he's only managed to strike such fear into the hearts of the oppressive upper class of his native major city state that he's been dubbed with a terrifying moniker. Most Solars in that time have already unzipped and worn their first Ebon Dragon as a coat, as I understand it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that at least 25% of them have learned Solar Sorcery too (another 25% do it in the second year).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:42:56-07:00","id":1239937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239924#post1239924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. They're not virtuous and righteous, but they are getting stuff done. It's arguable whether it's good (and, honestly, while Havesh may murder people, the Bull of the North has probably killed far, far more innocent people than Havesh has in his imperial war of conquest), but they are the sort of people you might choose to recruit in a war against the god-worlds who made the universe.<br /> <br /> I think the reason people bring them up with the Unconquered Sun choosing Solars is because of the logic chain:<br /> The Unconquered Sun is good;<br /> So he'd choose good people;<br /> He chooses bad people;<br /> This makes no sense.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the problem is him choosing people, I think the problem is assuming he's good, from the perspective of a 21st century player. He's Zeus/Ra/Jupiter/Huetzilopochtli. Sure, he's better than the Titans, but he's not perfect. So sometimes he chooses people who seem to others like villains.*<br /> (And Luna... is insane. And the Maidens are inscrutable and weird.)<br /> <br /> *Lyta literally was the villain for our Dragonblood game, but then, we were Dynasts, so maybe we were the villains. And I used Havesh as King of the Casteless in Varang, someone the PCs cooperated with as his revolution distracted the authorities from the PCs plans to rescue all Djala slaves, and later killed because he was also cooperating with people that Sidereals+Kes had manipulated them into fighting. Well, actually they killed him because he was a suspicious foreigner in their enemy's palace who was trying to leave and wouldn't answer their questions. That's PCs for you.<br /> <br /> Saying this, I was totally fine with the 2e thing of the Exaltations choosing people themselves, and I preferred that to the UCS choosing them. But I don't think it's a big problem.<br /> (As long as there's some mechanism for the Exaltations to keep choosing people after the UCS dies, of course, otherwise I'd have had to stop people making new Solar characters in my game. Or Lunar characters.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure that if the UCS died solar exaltations would remain, as we now have examples of other Chosen in 3e lore who have died off due to their patron dieing. IIRC in the Dev Q&amp;A they mentioned that to kill off exaltations required either complete removal of the being that was able to be exalted OR removal of the source of exaltation, but I could be misremembering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:48:14-07:00","id":1239940,"title":"","content":"That'd be really awkward, to be honest. I guess maybe it'd be okay if he could be replaced; maybe then the plot could be trying to find a replacement for him so that the Solars start exalting again.<br /> But I think it'd really encourage a lot of people who don't like Solars to try murdering the Sun, and I'm not sure I like that.<br /> <br /> Honestly, when I killed off the UCS, I didn't do it so that Solars would stop exalting, and the PCs would desperately need to replace him (I'm not sure they would anyway). The point was to have a world where Authocthon and his Sidereal servants ruled Yu-Shan instead of the UCS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T04:08:18-07:00","id":1239973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239940#post1239940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd be really awkward, to be honest. I guess maybe it'd be okay if he could be replaced; maybe then the plot could be trying to find a replacement for him so that the Solars start exalting again.<br /> But I think it'd really encourage a lot of people who don't like Solars to try murdering the Sun, and I'm not sure I like that.<br /> <br /> Honestly, when I killed off the UCS, I didn't do it so that Solars would stop exalting, and the PCs would desperately need to replace him (I'm not sure they would anyway). The point was to have a world where Authocthon and his Sidereal servants ruled Yu-Shan instead of the UCS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said there are more than a few reason's I dislike it. Also, the only examples we have of the UCS have been in 2e where he's been a shining paragon of everything good. I can't say I like it, but like it doesn't match at all with someone who'd exalt people who have no problem murdering everything in his way. Which is why I prefer it to be automatic and beyond his control. Like I said, I have no problem with them as solars. I do have a problem with the UCS, himself, picking against &quot;type&quot;. I personally, don't like the implications it has on the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T04:34:32-07:00","id":1239982,"title":"","content":"Even an automated Exaltation process is going to follow a criteria of worthiness that was set by the Unconquered Sun before the Primordial War. If the attitude was that he thought he might needed monsters to fight monsters back then, why can't it be his outlook now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T04:35:55-07:00","id":1239983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239973#post1239973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the only examples we have of the UCS have been in 2e where he's been a shining paragon of everything good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't the Dragon Kings used to do human sacrifice to him and he was like &quot;yeah, that's cool.&quot;?<br /> Also, he spends all his time playing games and has allowed Heaven to become corrupt.<br /> <br /> I mean, Morke (who, IIRC, wrote his background) did use a lot of words like &quot;righteous&quot; and &quot;virtuous&quot; to describe him, but also wrote him as quite clearly having irresponsibly abandoned his duties.<br /> <br /> Not saying that he's a monster, but neither was he presented as a 100% perfect guy. <br /> <br /> I do still agree with you to some extent though; certainly, the UCS choosing does imply some virtue or value in the Solars, beyond the &quot;they're someone who will try to change the world and not sit around doing nothing&quot; of 2nd ed. And I don't really want a morality test for PCs before they're even made (beyond that of the ST telling people not to play serial killers or something), not to mention I want to be able to use Solar villains.<br /> But I don't think it's a huge issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T04:39:50-07:00","id":1239984,"title":"","content":"Evil solars are like those villains in stories you can't help but like. <br /> <br /> &quot;Man, this dude is an asshole but he's <i>so cool</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, shit.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T05:06:14-07:00","id":1239990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239983#post1239983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the Dragon Kings used to do human sacrifice to him and he was like &quot;yeah, that's cool.&quot;?<br /> Also, he spends all his time playing games and has allowed Heaven to become corrupt.<br /> <br /> I mean, Morke (who, IIRC, wrote his background) did use a lot of words like &quot;righteous&quot; and &quot;virtuous&quot; to describe him, but also wrote him as quite clearly having irresponsibly abandoned his duties.<br /> <br /> Not saying that he's a monster, but neither was he presented as a 100% perfect guy.<br /> <br /> I do still agree with you to some extent though; certainly, the UCS choosing does imply some virtue or value in the Solars, beyond the &quot;they're someone who will try to change the world and not sit around doing nothing&quot; of 2nd ed. And I don't really want a morality test for PCs before they're even made (beyond that of the ST telling people not to play serial killers or something), not to mention I want to be able to use Solar villains.<br /> But I don't think it's a huge issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>The games were treated as something to migrate his overwhelming compassion and unless it was stated otherwise the sacrifices stopped when he changed. I mean he was the god of of all virtue essentially. Not a fan of it but it's currently the only thing we have on him. Even if he wasn't, I still don't like the idea of him handpicking people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T05:39:42-07:00","id":1239996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239983#post1239983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morke (who, IIRC, wrote his background) did use a lot of words like &quot;righteous&quot; and &quot;virtuous&quot; to describe him\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>He was also pretty quick to point out that the virtues weren't connected to any objective morals, and that righteousness in such a world equates to having physically or verbally beat the shit out of everyone else's arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239983#post1239983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026but also wrote him as quite clearly having irresponsibly abandoned his duties.</div> </div> </div> </div>M\u00f8rke was hardly the first; check <i>Games of Divinity</i> again - did the Unconquered Sun say, &quot;Let us slay our creators, and then immediately get back to work at the thankless jobs we didn't ask for!&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-29-2018, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T05:52:39-07:00","id":1239999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239937#post1239937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not sure that if the UCS died solar exaltations would remain, as we now have examples of other Chosen in 3e lore who have died off due to their patron dieing. IIRC in the Dev Q&amp;A they mentioned that to kill off exaltations required either complete removal of the being that was able to be exalted OR removal of the source of exaltation, but I could be misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are. Killing the Unconquered Sun would not stop the Solar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T06:39:17-07:00","id":1240014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239983#post1239983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but also wrote [the Unconquered Sun] as quite clearly having irresponsibly abandoned his duties.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be useful to view the Unconquered Sun through the lens of &quot;former slave who organized a slave revolt to free his people&quot; when looking at his relationship with his former duties.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the idea of the Incarnae being dangerously irresponsible only became entrenched after the game line switched over to the idea that Creation was in constant, imminent danger of annihilation from a thousand dooms. Third Edition has walked that back, allowing PCs to indulge in non-world-saving adventures without moral panic. This makes the question of how responsible or irresponsible the Incarnae are into something less dramatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T06:42:36-07:00","id":1240015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are. Killing the Unconquered Sun would not stop the Solar Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. That'd be awkward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239996#post1239996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was also pretty quick to point out that the virtues weren't connected to any objective morals, and that righteousness in such a world equates to having physically or verbally beat the shit out of everyone else's arguments.<br /> <br /> M\u00f8rke was hardly the first; check <i>Games of Divinity</i> again - did the Unconquered Sun say, &quot;Let us slay our creators, and then immediately get back to work at our thankless jobs!&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, I don't think the UCS has ever been presented as a perfect moral deity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean he was the god of of all virtue</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure someone can make a point about how one views virtue, but I'll point out that there's lots of gods who don't reflect their purview perfectly. Venus doesn't always make everyone happy, the God of Health isn't immune to Citrine Poxes of Contagion, Mercury sometimes has a rest, the God of Badgers is more intelligent than a badger, and the god of strength isn't infinitely strong.<br /> <br /> Even being the god of virtues doesn't actually make the UCS perfectly virtuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:58:01-07:00","id":1240050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1239931#post1239931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that Havesh is truly wasting his potential. Why, in the single, solitary year that he's been Exalted, he's only managed to strike such fear into the hearts of the oppressive upper class of his native major city state that he's been dubbed with a terrifying moniker. Most Solars in that time have already unzipped and worn their first Ebon Dragon as a coat, as I understand it.<br /> <br /> Never mind any of that stuff I said about how he seems to be gradually talking himself into being a champion for his fellow casteless; if you don't come to that conclusion immediately upon being given greater power and opportunity than you ever could have dreamed of in your previously extremely underprivileged life, you've missed your window for your entire, several millenia long lifespan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main point I was making is even if the Sun thinks osmeone will do something, good or not, it might be they don't. This is a big thing I think folks presume: The Sun gets exactly what he wants when Exalts someone (which as you note, Lyta and Havesh can be construed to as doing) or that maybe he got the person but they do their own thing. In that case, tough shit, no take-backs for the Sun. See the whole reason he turend hs face in the first place.<br /> <br /> Folks getting upset on the Sun somehow picking jackasses means the Sun is a jackass has a lot of leaps in logic that I was trying ot illustrate fall through in Lyta and Havesh if you do go around judging them for your actions, even though as you and other snote, even they might just be fine by the Sun anyhow. My complaints is folks seem to have this need to moralize the Sun today in a way apparently he wasnt' in th epast, and in ways which try to make <i>their</i> Exaltations less legitimate/worthy because he went and Exalted those assholes over there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:20:37-07:00","id":1240056,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think of the worst Solars from the Time of Tumult that we've ever actually gotten in the Time of Tumult, and the worst that I can recall are people who somewhat prioritise things of abstract or aesthetic value over the lives and livelihood of other people in Creation, which is not the best, but also far from the worst villains that one can envision, or see at work in the rest of the Time of Tumult.<br /> <br /> I mean, the worst thing that I can think of about Arianna is something along the lines of her viewing people around her as less worthwhile than the kinds of things that she might discover or envision or create as she comes into her power. That's kind of obnoxious, but not exactly harmful, and there might be something to be said for the value of the things that she might create. Some of the greatest artists in history have been kind of conceited jerks to actually know, and when this didn't extend to things like actually being severely abusive in their personal lives or outright tyrannical in their professional conduct, I don't think that exactly detracts from the value of their art.<br /> <br /> Havesh, sure he sees the power that he's been recently granted as finally the chance to get his, but that's still specifically via means of taking it away from the mouths of his former oppressors, rather than joining their ranks and growing fat on the system. Having sex with people under false identities is a violation, but within the very specific context of this story's premises and supernatural details, something that I think is worth examining in terms of being less actively violent than other means of violation. I'll certainly say that the image of a kind of trickster thief that slays the rich and sleeps with their wives is the kind of thing that peasants and commoners throughout most of history would probably laugh it*.<br /> <br /> Yurgen Kaneko? If we still go by his write-up in Caste Book: Dawn, he's a weary old man that was given a new lease on life, and is struggling to decide what to make of it. Sure, he's engaging in a campaign of imperial conquest in a similar model to the Mongols, but the thing that I find in both of those cases that strikes me as a bit different from other models of imperial conquest is that they're not exactly coming from an advantaged background that makes their conquest a form of punching down.<br /> <br /> I think there's a noteworthy difference between certain kinds of European imperialism, in which a society that benefits from geographic and circumstantial advantages becomes exceedingly rich, and out of a need for ever expanding revenue streams, direct access to natural resources, and a general sense of entitlement, starts stealing countries, and a society in which a widely distributed but culturally related people are struggling to scrape together a living in barely arable steppe land (or tundra, as the case may be), such that they're forced to constantly fight amongst themselves to accumulate basic resources, who ultimately have a figure who is able to knock them all into line and say &quot;we're surrounded by people who thrive off of having so much more than us, at the moment they're experiencing a moment of vulnerability, and the fact that we're conditioned to live and breathe war means that as a fully united front, we're capable of overpowering them; let's take some things to make life less of a struggle&quot;. In the case of the actual Mongols, one might argue that such a motivating factor may have been part of why their attitude towards conquered territories that relented was more accommodating than might be typical of imperialism (and even the mass murder kind of existed in a calculation where their numbers and lifestyle did not exactly support sustained occupation of major holdouts of opposition, which is not exactly good, but I think needs to be considered a bit from the viewpoint of the people doing it).<br /> <br /> So when the matter of some Solars being monsters comes up, I'm often left with the question of exactly what they've done and who they're doing it to, and if they might ultimately be using their powers in less objectionable ways than many of the other powers of the latter Second Age, that grow fat off of the exploitation of the under classes?<br /> <br /> One thing that I'll say might advantage Solars over the likes of the Scarlet Dynasty and the Guild; offhand, I cannot recall any book depicting a Solar that has grown wealthy off of the acquisition and trade of enslaved people.<br /> <br /> * There is an intrinsic underlying misogyny to the premise of things like Havesh viewing the wives of his marks as a kind of prize, that to sleep with them constitutes a final insult to the memory of those marks, and to the general assumption that his wealthy victims have spouses in the role of kept women, but that's more an unexamined assumption that goes into the writing rather than a specific trait of the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:52:17-07:00","id":1240065,"title":"","content":"But do you think that their actions are not quite so monstrous because the Solar exaltation/Unconquered Sun actively seeks out good (or better-than-average) people, or because most people who are bad in some ways are actually complex characters whose motivations do make some sense in context?<br /> So that whenever there's a bad Solar, their views and actions do make some sense based on their social position, background, psychology, etc, but this would also be true for a bad Lunar, bad Dragonblood, bad Liminal, bad Sidereal, bad Exigent or bad mortal?<br /> <br /> Like... I used to live in a country ruled by a dictator (who's just abolished term limits), whose sister has a suspiciously large fortune, who cracks down on dissent, has people imprisoned for criticising him or the political system, etc. The prison in my city was full of people whose only crime was to belong to a religion that became too popular. I have friends banned from being involved in politics or a high rank in the civil service because of their religion. And I've read of far worse on the news (I just don't know anyone personally who's been arrested/killed).<br /> <br /> But if you look at his background (he grew up in a period of anarchy), history, etc, you can argue that he really believes that what his country really needs is a strong, hard leader, and he can't give up power because the friends of those he arrested for corruption will come after him (and, okay, his sister might be hella corrupt, but how many of us would arrest our own family?).<br /> I think he's a bad guy, but his actions can be justified from a certain point of view. Like most bad people.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm saying is the fact that Lyta and Havesh's actions can be justified from a certain point of view isn't proof that Solars are chosen with moral standards in a way that Dragonblood aren't, but just that they're well-written and realistically portrayed. A Solar who's just a serial killer who loves killing people because they love evil would be very dull.<br /> <br /> I would say, overall, Solars probably <i>are</i> better morally than Dragonblood (whose exaltation isn't chosen by anyone), but that's because many Dragonblood were born in lives of privilege built on imperialism, with a religion that encourages them to think they're better than others, not because the UCS chooses Solars he thinks will be good.<br /> <br /> (I mean, it'd make sense for the UCS to choose them that way; but I think the implication that Solars were chosen because he thought they were good people would be awkward for the game)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-29-2018, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:13:00-07:00","id":1240080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240056#post1240056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think of the worst Solars from the Time of Tumult that we've ever actually gotten in the Time of Tumult, and the worst that I can recall are people who somewhat prioritise things of abstract or aesthetic value over the lives and livelihood of other people in Creation, which is not the best, but also far from the worst villains that one can envision, or see at work in the rest of the Time of Tumult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there was that one Solar out East. I can't remember if it was Rathess or a different city, but he's got a bunch of feral Dragon Kings for lackeys. He worships some ancient god of decay, disease, cannibalism, or something like that. The Solar has the Dragon Kings round up anyone captured nearby, and sacrifices them to that god. I'd label him as pretty far down on the totem of sanity! The god himself was said to be an enemy of heaven, so yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:27:44-07:00","id":1240088,"title":"","content":"His name is Filial Wisdom, and yes it is in Rathess. He's a good villain for a mid-level circle of Celestial PCs, or a higher-ranked circle of Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> I suspect he's too wacky to return in 3rd edition though. We shall see. <br /> (Or not; more likely he just won't be mentioned)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:34:41-07:00","id":1240095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240065#post1240065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But do you think that their actions are not quite so monstrous because the Solar exaltation/Unconquered Sun actively seeks out good (or better-than-average) people, or because most people who are bad in some ways are actually complex characters whose motivations do make some sense in context?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can model it as two basic things. One is that the criteria for selecting Solars excludes people that would be severely greedy, virulently anti-social, or reactionary in a manner that would persecute the underprivileged.<br /> <br /> The other is that the kind of power that one can possess as a Solar strikes me as being something that can be somewhat liberating from things such as fear that the oppressed and marginalized will drag you from your home and pillory you, or that the advancement of your own benefits rests on the exploitation of those beneath you.<br /> <br /> There may still be cases in which you get Solars who privilege their own in-group over any others, and prosecute war on their behalf (which is unlike the Realm, whose imperialism is not predicated on nationalism), but I would also think the dynamics of such may intersect with the prior points in ways distinct from much of reality. I also think that privileging one's in-group may only go so far; I propose that a person whose tribalism is based on a highly irrational bigotry, such as a White Nationalist, would not be Chosen as a Solar under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that whenever there's a bad Solar, their views and actions do make some sense based on their social position, background, psychology, etc, but this would also be true for a bad Lunar, bad Dragonblood, bad Liminal, bad Sidereal, bad Exigent or bad mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>My point in the other post isn't really about whether being bad makes sense, but rather to examine their conduct and their targets and think about what this might say about power dynamics and how that might inform motivations.<br /> <br /> The motivation behind converting human beings into property and profiting dramatically off of them makes sense, but I'm questioning whether or not it's a motivation that would be present in Solars, and what that says about the kind of harm that they cause.<br /> <br /> However, my point is not ultimately on whether or not any given Solar is a better person than a given Dragon Blood, just whether or not their actions cause more harm, questioning who they're causing it to, and whether they're people that deserve it less.<br /> <br /> (I don't think my actual world and moral view is so consequentialist, insofar as I understand the philosophy, but I think it's a consideration for examining the different Exalted)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like... I used to live in a country ruled by a dictator (who's just abolished term limits), whose sister has a suspiciously large fortune, who cracks down on dissent, has people imprisoned for criticising him or the political system, etc. The prison in my city was full of people whose only crime was to belong to a religion that became too popular. I have friends banned from being involved in politics or a high rank in the civil service because of their religion. And I've read of far worse on the news (I just don't know anyone personally who's been arrested/killed).<br /> <br /> But if you look at his background (he grew up in a period of anarchy), history, etc, you can argue that he really believes that what his country really needs is a strong, hard leader, and he can't give up power because the friends of those he arrested for corruption will come after him (and, okay, his sister might be hella corrupt, but how many of us would arrest our own family?).<br /> I think he's a bad guy, but his actions can be justified from a certain point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess what I'm saying is that Solars might not necessarily be expected to embark upon these courses, because they're less vulnerable to negative outcomes, and can potentially develop stronger alternative means of dealing with them.<br /> <br /> It's like, implications that Vladimir Putin lives in mortal terror of being dragged out of his home, brutally and humiliatingly tortured in public, and executed make a kind of sense, because no matter how good his exercise regimen or martial arts training is, he's still a mortal man, and can be easily overpowered if he's trapped alone with something like five or more people, preferably armed. There's a discussion about whether there's anything reasonable in responding to that fear by trying to be less of a man who might be subject to such revolution, and the morality underlying actions taken while perceiving oneself (possibly accurately) to be trapped in a situation in which relinquishing power is liable to be a death sentence (which I think speaks a lot to many historical dynastic power struggles and policies), but that might be a bit beyond the scope of this discussion.<br /> <br /> For the time being, I'm suggesting that a Solar, not totally invulnerable, but perhaps considerably less vulnerable, might not feel incentives towards the same kinds of oppression.<br /> <br /> I think the Dragon Blooded live less in fear of their mortal populace than they do one another and existential threats from the edges and outside of the world, but I think the result is still largely the same in having created highly exploitative and widespread social systems based on privileging the few in order to maximize their power against such threats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like most bad people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most bad people are just conditioned to entitlement and indifference to the lives of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying is the fact that Lyta and Havesh's actions can be justified from a certain point of view isn't proof that Solars are chosen with moral standards in a way that Dragonblood aren't, but just that they're well-written and realistically portrayed. A Solar who's just a serial killer who loves killing people because they love evil would be very dull.<br /> <br /> I would say, overall, Solars probably <i>are</i> better morally than Dragonblood (whose exaltation isn't chosen by anyone), but that's because many Dragonblood were born in lives of privilege built on imperialism, with a religion that encourages them to think they're better than others, not because the UCS chooses Solars he thinks will be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>My priority is less on justification than on questioning and examining the assumption that they represent contrary examples that either undermine a heroic thesis to the Solar Exalted (particularly if it's supposed to be chosen personally by the Sun), or presents Solar Exaltation as wholly amoral.<br /> <br /> It's also a bit of a re-examination of my generally questioning the assumption that Solars are inclined to become oppressive overlords.<br /> <br /> Plus a few other things, like my ongoing quest to form a coherent argument against the assertion that the founder of the Guild would have been appropriate for an Eclipse Caste Exaltation if one had been available, and developing a basis for differentiating Solars from Abyssals and Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:50:35-07:00","id":1240104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240080#post1240080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there was that one Solar out East. I can't remember if it was Rathess or a different city, but he's got a bunch of feral Dragon Kings for lackeys. He worships some ancient god of decay, disease, cannibalism, or something like that. The Solar has the Dragon Kings round up anyone captured nearby, and sacrifices them to that god. I'd label him as pretty far down on the totem of sanity! The god himself was said to be an enemy of heaven, so yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'd forgotten almost entirely about Filial Wisdom. I'm not really sure where to place him in an examination of the Solar Exalted, because he's extremely weird and kind of marginal.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit torn about his relationship with Han-Tha; on principle, I maintain the significance of Solars being open to the influence of others rather than being entirely enclosed and open to no will but their own, but association with that god seems to so thoroughly undermine any meaningful agency or personality to Filial Wisdom at all...<br /> <br /> I guess he counts as the most unpleasant Solar by default, but even then it's not only off-kilter, but kind of self-contained (as I recall, all that he's really doing is presiding over a kingdom of monsters, and is only particularly threatening to people that stumble across him), that I'm left questioning whether he's substantially monstrous, or just mostly carries the look.<br /> <br /> I don't know. I kind of want to discount him altogether, but also fear that to do so is to just be a matter of saying &quot;this doesn't support my thesis, so it doesn't count&quot;.<br /> <br /> The best that I can think of for the moment is that he's an edge case, and one that says more about apprehension over the power of the Solars being wielded on behalf of malefic but compelling beings than something that says very much about the Solars themselves.<br /> <br /> I suppose even that has to accommodate the idea that, after taking the Second Breath, Lyta could conceivably fall under the influence of somebody that convinces her to burn the poor (especially given my overall principle of reinforcing that no Solar is an island), which certainly makes things more complicated, but would at least maintain an idea that they're not singular wills indelibly charting their own course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T10:33:36-07:00","id":1240121,"title":"","content":"I think you could certainly argue that Filial Wisdom might have started out good, but been corrupted over time by Han-Tha.<br /> While Solars being chosen with some kind of moral criteria isn't something I like, I don't think the existence of Filial Wisdom disproves it. He's had over 100 years of being the only Solar he's ever known or met, and for much of that he hasn't even interacted with humans that much. It'd make anyone crack. That's before adding Han-Tha.<br /> <br /> To get back to the central idea...<br /> Does Solars being chosen with morals in mind apply to other Celestials chosen by patrons? Ie Lunars and Sidereals? Or purely Solars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T11:01:31-07:00","id":1240141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240121#post1240121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Solars being chosen with morals in mind apply to other Celestials chosen by patrons? Ie Lunars and Sidereals? Or purely Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unconquered Sun is a war god so he's okay with killing in various contexts, but I don't know that he'd be able to fall in love with a sociopathic serial killer like BTK or John Gacy if he knew what sort of a person they were. The Unconquered Sun, of course, isn't omniscient so he might see a John Gacy type character doing something good or impressive and Exalt that person without ever realizing that the guy is a horrible serial killer with a basement full of dead children.<br /> <br /> Luna however has been presented as fickle but also a much darker being than the Unconquered Sun, so it seems reasonable to me that she could intentionally Exalt a mass murdering serial killer, viewing them as a &quot;hunter of humans&quot; in a a way that would make her deem that person worthy of Exaltation.<br /> <br /> As for the Maidens, it depends on how much control they have over their Exaltations. In some ways they've been presented as doing things because Samsara says they will do them, so if Samsara says they will Exalted person X that's what they're going to do. At the same time though, Sidereal are expected to work in a hierarchy alongside a lot of other people, so I imagine they would prefer not to Exalt true sociopaths who are have a difficult time feeling affinity for other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-29-2018, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T11:01:47-07:00","id":1240143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240121#post1240121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Solars being chosen with morals in mind</div> </div> </div> </div>I still feel that we're not quite on the same page; that I'm not so much arguing that they're Chosen because they're moral, but that distinctly immoral people, people that could be reasonably assumed to go directly to using their power for their own benefit at the expense of people that are already at the bottom of the social ladder, or strongly infringe upon the lives of people at large, or simply express some venomous or antisocial hangups, would not be.<br /> <br /> At the same time as I'm arguing that the likes of Lyta and Havesh aren't quite as bad as they're made out to be (or at least aren't bad in the ways and for the reasons that many assume), with a small reference to Arianna hardly being bad at all.<br /> <br /> (One person whose write-up I would quite like to examine again is Ophiles Ses)<br /> <br /> I should also reiterate that my motive in assessing the criteria for selecting Solars and the manner in which they might conduct is constantly labouring under the need to distinguish them from what they are when fully corrupted by the Great Curse (in a manner more sophisticated than the corrupted Solars being ridiculously evil, and something that actually connects to how it works mechanically).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">apply to other Celestials chosen by patrons? Ie Lunars and Sidereals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have a duty to preserve the existence of the world while personally existing somewhat apart from it, that is bestowed upon them at birth, and that they're conditioned to for their entire lives up until Exaltation. I think that's a firm foundation for the majority of them consistently being... well, dedicated to an authority and interests outside of themselves, at least, and generally beneficial, even if the principles that they serve can be somewhat amoral.<br /> <br /> I currently think that the imperative behind Choosing Lunars is to bestow them with freedom, or at least a greater capacity for the pursuit of their own freedom. I do think that can say a lot about their possible backgrounds and how those might inform character, but overall feel that they should contain the greatest diversity in personality and aspirations among the Celestial Exalted, and be more accommodating to people that are primarily concerned with pursuit of their own interests. Even if I imagine that their powers will generally afford them a means of simply acquiring what they want directly, rather than generating systems for it.<br /> <br /> I think that there are legitimate implications to this that would make it a good thing that they cleaved to the Solars and adopted a role as guardians, and for the Sidereals to be nervous about the implications of a world in which they are unfettered and hold the mastery.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I'll also note that if I'm being led by example in assessment of the various kinds of Exalted, many of the Lunars are up to their necks in creating and benefiting from systems designed to exploit vulnerable people. They're not doing it in precisely the manner of the Scarlet Dynasty, of exploiting their labour to enrich themselves, but there is definitely a widespread trend among the Lunars for radicalising people that have been harmed by the Realm's policies and then expending those people to secure incremental advantages. I would definitely think that there are many Lunars, and possibly not exactly old Lunars, that have done more harm to more people that had enough to deal with already for their own benefit than Havesh or Lyta have.<br /> <br /> I don't condemn them for that, partially because I can sufficiently distance myself and partially because I sympathise with their position a little bit, but it would inform my perspective of the criteria of them being Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-29-2018, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T12:03:23-07:00","id":1240159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240143#post1240143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still feel that we're not quite on the same page; that I'm not so much arguing that they're Chosen because they're moral, but that distinctly immoral people, people that could be reasonably assumed to go directly to using their power for their own benefit at the expense of people that are already at the bottom of the social ladder, or strongly infringe upon the lives of people at large, or simply express some venomous or antisocial hangups, would not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, to be honest you're right. So many people come into these threads arguing so many nuances, that you can end up responding to a whole bunch of semi-linked-stuff in a way that's directed to one person who's only expressed some of those points.<br /> <br /> And I realised that, honestly, I don't really have anything against, say, serial killers not becoming Solars. I'd neither want a PC to play one or particularly want to have one as an NPC.<br /> I just somewhat dislike the idea that there's some kind of moral baseline that applies to Solars and not to others, because I think it leads to people thinking the Solars are the good guys of the setting, because, well, they're more good. While the Dragonblood and Lunars may cause more problems for the world (currently), I'd prefer that this is clearly due to their socio-cultural-economic circumstances, rather than because Solars are &quot;the good guys&quot;.<br /> But as long as the baseline is low enough that I can have Solar thieves, Solar assassins, Solar tyrants, and Solar fanatics, it isn't really a problem, practically speaking. I don't really want to run Solar NPCs, or many NPCs generally, who are simply moustache-twirling evil. But I don't want players saying &quot;this Solar antagonist is just too evil, he'd never have been exalted.&quot; Or saying that for each others' characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (One person whose write-up I would quite like to examine again is Ophiles Ses) </div> </div> </div>I do like Ophilis Ses. Of the 4 or 5 Nexus Solars, I think he was the most interesting.<br /> The Twilight in my game made a diamond ring for Azure Path (Ses's boyfriend) to propose to him with.<br /> Ses later became King of Nexus. He wasn't a perfect king, but better than the Council of Entities. (How much difference is there between a successful crime gang that does protection rackets, and a King? Especially when you're in a crime gang because it's your family background and how you were raised, as opposed to you just love stealing and hurting people).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I should also reiterate that my motive in assessing the criteria for selecting Solars and the manner in which they might conduct is constantly labouring under the need to distinguish them from what they are when fully corrupted by the Great Curse (in a manner more sophisticated than the corrupted Solars being ridiculously evil, and something that actually connects to how it works mechanically). </div> </div> </div>I don't quite understand what you mean by that, could you elaborate?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-29-2018, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T13:00:19-07:00","id":1240184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240159#post1240159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just somewhat dislike the idea that there's some kind of moral baseline that applies to Solars and not to others, because I think it leads to people thinking the Solars are the good guys of the setting, because, well, they're more good.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are mostly things that I'm extrapolating and developing in a direction of my own liking; they're not really things that I would expect or particularly want to be explicit.<br /> <br /> That said, I also find that in the absence of any such arguments or details, people seem to lean towards presuming that Solars are amoral, uncontrollable monsters in their own right. There's just <i>so much</i> of a background of people generally referring to them as mind-controlling tyrants. I'm searching for something in a different direction, that I think has more variety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the Dragonblood and Lunars may cause more problems for the world (currently), I'd prefer that this is clearly due to their socio-cultural-economic circumstances, rather than because Solars are &quot;the good guys&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, think about how among the things that I'm saying is that the powers of the Solar Exalted might liberate them from some of the constraints or incentives of such circumstances. Not intrinsically better, but privileged with the means to not be weighed down by these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as long as the baseline is low enough that I can have Solar thieves, Solar assassins, Solar tyrants, and Solar fanatics, it isn't really a problem, practically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but the latter two raise questions to me; what is the nature of their tyranny, their fanaticism? What do they want, and why, and how are they going about trying to get it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't quite understand what you mean by that, could you elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want the Solars at the end of the First Age to be distinct, and a plausibly threat to the existence of the world. I want this to be a thing that comes organically with the way that the Great Curse works in play. I want it to be meaningfully distinct from a Solar that is going about in the manner of an ancient world conqueror or political schemer, and I want it to be more sophisticated that just turning people into meat trees on a whim.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T16:28:44-07:00","id":1240238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240143#post1240143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(One person whose write-up I would quite like to examine again is Ophiles Ses)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was <i>just</i> rereading <i>CB:Night</i>, and I noticed, <i>all</i> the <i>Night </i>Castes in that first chapter got a message from the Unconquered Sun in the way that <i>Zeniths </i>are supposed to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:46:03-07:00","id":1240294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240238#post1240238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was <i>just</i> rereading <i>CB:Night</i>, and I noticed, <i>all</i> the <i>Night </i>Castes in that first chapter got a message from the Unconquered Sun in the way that <i>Zeniths </i>are supposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I kind of like allowing it as an option for non-Zeniths. Like, Zeniths get special attention, but sometimes you just take a shine to someone. So to speak.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the little subargument about the nature of the Sun: he is not a perfectly moral being. Never has been. He may be a perfectly virtuous being, but they're the virtues of Socrates and Aristotle, not the seven virtues of Catholic philosophy. There should be a little moral ambiguity at every step, even as the options for, say, continued human existence are probably those favored.<br /> <br /> The Sun led a slave revolt, true. But on the other hand, the Primordials were cosmic beings to whom the Sun and his kin were, like, their working dogs. It's not good to mistreat such an animal, but you wouldn't let it have a vote.<br /> <br /> The Incarna play the Games of Divinity and neglect their duties, but on the other hand they never had a say in taking those duties, see aforementioned slavery.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation was probably necessary to keep Solars from wrecking the world, but it forever lessened it. The point here is there are often no <i>objectively correct</i> answers, just ones that happened to be the answers chosen.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:11:16-07:00","id":1240303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240159#post1240159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as long as the baseline is low enough that I can have Solar thieves, Solar assassins, Solar tyrants, and Solar fanatics, it isn't really a problem, practically speaking. I don't really want to run Solar NPCs, or many NPCs generally, who are simply moustache-twirling evil. But I don't want players saying &quot;this Solar antagonist is just too evil, he'd never have been exalted.&quot; Or saying that for each others' characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been of the opinion that none of the Incarnae will choose someone of evil character. Rather they choose individuals who have something to offer Creation. None of the Incarnae are going to exalt a psychopathic serial killer, or rapist, or a genocidal tyrant. This is reinforced by the fact that we have dozens of examples of people exalted by the Incarnae, and none of them started out as &quot;moustache-twirling evil&quot; individuals. However, it is entirely possible that their power and circumstances turn them evil after exaltation (example Filial Wisdom). As for your list of wanting Solar's that are assassins and thieves, this is literally the archetype of the Night caste. Tyrants and fanatics are more of the gray area, because it depends on a lot of different factors. For instance, I don't see any of the Incarnae exalting a Tyrant despot who takes joy in oppressing and torturing his subject. However, a tyrant that cracks down on his kingdom to enforce stability and conquers surrounding kingdoms in brutal warfare, is someone the Incarnae might find useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T00:48:15-07:00","id":1240347,"title":"","content":"Yeah, statistically speaking I think a Tyrant-king is most likely to exalt as an abyssal after they get assassinated than either of the other solaroids. <br /> <br /> Cos, like, Infernals are supposed to be downtrodden people who go &quot;who's laughing now&quot;, usurp their former oppressors with infernal might and <i>then</i> become tyrant kings. <br /> <br /> And I think the situation is largely the same for solars. Every solar <i>could</i> have become a righteous exemplar after their exaltation, using their powers to better the world. Some don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:01:57-07:00","id":1240356,"title":"","content":"I feel that statistics should not have anything to do with who gets Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:11:12-07:00","id":1240360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240303#post1240303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always been of the opinion that none of the Incarnae will choose someone of evil character. Rather they choose individuals who have something to offer Creation. None of the Incarnae are going to exalt a psychopathic serial killer, or rapist, or a genocidal tyrant. This is reinforced by the fact that we have dozens of examples of people exalted by the Incarnae, and none of them started out as &quot;moustache-twirling evil&quot; individuals. However, it is entirely possible that their power and circumstances turn them evil after exaltation (example Filial Wisdom). As for your list of wanting Solar's that are assassins and thieves, this is literally the archetype of the Night caste. Tyrants and fanatics are more of the gray area, because it depends on a lot of different factors. For instance, I don't see any of the Incarnae exalting a Tyrant despot who takes joy in oppressing and torturing his subject. However, a tyrant that cracks down on his kingdom to enforce stability and conquers surrounding kingdoms in brutal warfare, is someone the Incarnae might find useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't think that they should get a say in the matter. Someone who exalted just needs to have some innate quality that drives them, even if they are evil and havesh was definitely a rapist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:52:07-07:00","id":1240369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240294#post1240294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the little subargument about the nature of the Sun: he is not a perfectly moral being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can at least see the argument, not so much in terms of &quot;the Unconquered Sun is supposed to be perfectly moral, and having a direct hand in Exalting bad people damages that&quot;, but rather that if the Unconquered Sun chooses people that were either bad at the time, or a discerning individual might reasonably expect them to turn so, that he's morally culpable for the acts of those Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240303#post1240303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">their power and circumstances turn them evil after exaltation (example Filial Wisdom).</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, I can't properly bring up my copy of Ruins of Rathess at the moment, so I want to ask again: is Filial Wisdom actually doing something, or does he just kind of carry the aesthetic markers of fantasy evil?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240360#post1240360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even if they are evil and havesh was definitely a rapist.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is a rapist, but not quite in the manner that I'd say most people think of if it's said on its own.<br /> <br /> It definitely makes him a criminal, and a person who has wronged others by exploiting their trust and their ignorance, in a manner that is a violation.<br /> <br /> But I'm also the kind of person who thinks that designating rape with the specific word &quot;evil&quot;, which carries a lot of cultural baggage, is to put the concept on a pedestal, giving it more grandeur than it deserves or is good for effective social response to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T03:28:43-07:00","id":1240377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240369#post1240369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I'm also the kind of person who thinks that designating rape with the specific word &quot;evil&quot;, which carries a lot of cultural baggage, is to put the concept on a pedestal, giving it more grandeur than it deserves or is good for effective social response to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to put evil in quotes but I don't know. I mean it's a hard thing to quantify.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T03:50:11-07:00","id":1240382,"title":"","content":"We have seen from Panther that the sun occasionally exalts people who he feels could be doing better things with their life. Some, like Panther, live up to it. <br /> <br /> Some don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T04:48:43-07:00","id":1240389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240360#post1240360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't think that they should get a say in the matter. Someone who exalted just needs to have some innate quality that drives them, even if they are evil and havesh was definitely a rapist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Havesh didn't do his whole Vanisher schtick <b>before</b> he Exalted, which is an important distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T04:52:26-07:00","id":1240390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240382#post1240382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the sun occasionally exalts people who he feels could be doing better things with their life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their life that is extended to three thousand years. How far into that is it reasonable to look at somebody that has squandered their potential?<br /> <br /> Still, Havesh putting the fear of God into the hearts of the Varangian upper class is arguably a better use of his life than being a petty criminal and tourist guide in the gutter.<br /> <br /> And then a year into that, he flees into the wilderness after being exposed to the Wyld Hunt (I recall no reference to him exacting vengeance on the woman who turned him in), so who knows where he would go from there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T05:47:51-07:00","id":1240399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240369#post1240369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can at least see the argument, not so much in terms of &quot;the Unconquered Sun is supposed to be perfectly moral, and having a direct hand in Exalting bad people damages that&quot;, but rather that if the Unconquered Sun chooses people that were either bad at the time, or a discerning individual might reasonably expect them to turn so, that he's morally culpable for the acts of those Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, if choosing Exalts is a somewhat unconscious, autonomous thing - as said, it's been likened to &quot;falling in love&quot; - if you fall in love with someone who turns out to be evil, are you culpable for <i>their</i> acts? Perhaps if, while blinded by love, you took an action that turned out to be unwise, but it's not necessarily the same thing as cold-minded rationalized aiding and abetting, there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T06:11:32-07:00","id":1240408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240360#post1240360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't think that they should get a say in the matter. Someone who exalted just needs to have some innate quality that drives them, even if they are evil and havesh was definitely a rapist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we know the gods do choose their exalts this edition. Arguing otherwise is pointless. As for Havesh being a rapist, as I said, this is something that developed after he exalts. Also, he's not a rapist in the sense that most of us think of the term. He disguises himself like wealthy people so well, their wives/lovers don't know it's not the real person, and they willingly have sex with him. Yes, it's still a disgusting thing to do, but it's nothing like what we typically consider rape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240369#post1240369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, I can't properly bring up my copy of Ruins of Rathess at the moment, so I want to ask again: is Filial Wisdom actually doing something, or does he just kind of carry the aesthetic markers of fantasy evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he's running a cult to a fairly evil god, who's on the run from heaven. He's also sacrificing multiple people to this god. The book implies that while he's been in Rathess a while, he didn't grow up there. He may not be evil, but he's a pawn of evil and is so far gone morally, the best thing to do is kill him off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T06:49:40-07:00","id":1240414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240389#post1240389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havesh didn't do his whole Vanisher schtick <b>before</b> he Exalted, which is an important distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much of one. He exalted while <i>botching</i> his first assassination attempt. His inspiration for the Vanisher schtick came when he was almost caught by the young wife of his <i>second</i> victim, and he instinctively disguised himself and thus stumbled into the idea of preying on the wealthy to enjoy their luxury lifestyle for a while before needing to vanish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-30-2018, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T06:59:51-07:00","id":1240418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240414#post1240414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much of one. He exalted while <i>botching</i> his first assassination attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>He messed up by not realizing the guy was armored, but he very much succeeded in killing him. <br /> <br /> If we're gonna start framing every plan where one or two things go even a little bit wrong in the otherwise-successful undertaking a &quot;botch,&quot; that's gonna make discussing heist movies pretty awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-30-2018, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:01:20-07:00","id":1240419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives#post1238822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question! Does the core book talk about Solar reincarnation and past lives, or memories of the first age? I'm having a flick through and I haven't found much so far in any of the sections I'd have expected to talk about it.<br /> <br /> I'm familiar with how it works in previous editions, just wanted to know how / if this one tackles it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually asked Eric Minton about this on our latest episode! Give it a listen and see what he says. I personally found it both illuminating and a little frustrating, if I'm honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:31:41-07:00","id":1240424,"title":"","content":"Huh, there's a lot here, so I'll try not to become too disjointed in my responses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240303#post1240303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your list of wanting Solar's that are assassins and thieves, this is literally the archetype of the Night caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Bad people defined by their evil deeds. <br /> And I don't think it'd work well for the game to not allow assassins to be chosen as Solars. Including Yozi-worshipping assassins like Harmonious Jade, who kills people for her demonic masters, and then once they turn on her kills people for money instead.<br /> (Ranlea of Gem also kills people for money. She's a Dawn, not a Night, so this isn't exclusively a Dawn thing)<br /> <br /> I suppose you could argue that maybe the UCS chooses them because he thinks they're really skilled and could potentially become mighty heroes. That's fine.<br /> <br /> I guess I don't hate the idea that the UCS chooses people that he thinks have the potential to be great heroes, but sometimes he makes a mistake and they become great villains instead, as Elfive said.<br /> (And this causes him to get depressed)<br /> As long as there's the potential for me to run bad Solar NPCs (or have people play bad Solar PCs!).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the little subargument about the nature of the Sun: he is not a perfectly moral being. Never has been. He may be a perfectly virtuous being, but they're the virtues of Socrates and Aristotle, not the seven virtues of Catholic philosophy. There should be a little moral ambiguity at every step, even as the options for, say, continued human existence are probably those favored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your first point, but I think even saying he's a perfectly virtuous being is probably not true. Being the god of virtues may make him quite virtuous, but not necessarily perfectly virtuous, just as the goddess of serenity isn't perfectly serene, the goddess of peace isn't perfectly peaceful, and the god of health isn't perfectly healthy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Partly, because that makes roleplaying him if PCs turn up incredibly difficult. I mean, it's okay if he's subjectively virtuous according to his own opinion and point of view, but I don't think an ST, not being an objectively virtuous person, could pick the objectively virtuous thing for him to do in every situation the PCs present him with.<br /> <br /> Like... the PCs in my game were once chosen by him as judges in a trial. Another circle of Solars had killed Chejop Kejak and given his head to the Sun as a sacrifice. Ignis appointed the PCs judges. Is that the virtuous thing, reclusing himself, or the unvirtuous thing, giving someone else the responsibility? And if he had judged the PCs, could I myself, the ST, choose the objectively virtuous result for him to enforce? It's a difficult and complicated situation. Could I give a perfectly compassionate, temperate, valorous decision while also sticking to the UCS' convictions perfectly? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I also find that in the absence of any such arguments or details, people seem to lean towards presuming that Solars are amoral, uncontrollable monsters in their own right. There's just <i>so much</i> of a background of people generally referring to them as mind-controlling tyrants. I'm searching for something in a different direction, that I think has more variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmm... I mean, with the Great Curse 2nd edition First Age Solars, sure. I don't generally see people saying it about Time of Tumult Solars now, in 3rd edition. Partly because there's hardly any mind-control charms (I think that makes a big difference).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, think about how among the things that I'm saying is that the powers of the Solar Exalted might liberate them from some of the constraints or incentives of such circumstances. Not intrinsically better, but privileged with the means to not be weighed down by these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I've got no problem with saying that Solars, say, don't fear disease or poverty so much so may not feel as much pressure to make moral compromises. But that's not really related to saying the UCS doesn't choose really bad people (you could argue he's okay choosing bad people because he thinks being Solars might make them better).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havesh didn't do his whole Vanisher schtick before he exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. The UCS couldn't have known that's what he'd do. Or that he'd murder his own brother minutes after exalting in case he talked.<br /> <br /> Of course, Havesh did exalt while murdering an old man for money. Not the sort of thing you'd assume the UCS would consider a righteous act.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder... if the UCS chooses people, how much does he know? How often does he make mistakes and exalt someone he thought wasn't evil, when they were?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:32:12-07:00","id":1240425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240418#post1240418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He messed up by not realizing the guy was armored, but he very much succeeded in killing him.</div> </div> </div> </div>He succeeded <i>because</i> he exalted in the process of finding it rather difficult to strangle the old man.<br /> <br /> The best face you can put on it was that he was tenacious in the face of adversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-30-2018, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:16:17-07:00","id":1240440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240184#post1240184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, but the latter two raise questions to me; what is the nature of their tyranny, their fanaticism? What do they want, and why, and how are they going about trying to get it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fulgens Cruciatus, the Dawn in my group, believes that true morality is the strength to protect your people. If you win, you are good, if you lose, you are evil. Once he decapitated a prisoner I'd just taken then mocked me for not keeping my word (because I'd told the prisoner that if he talked, we wouldn't kill him).<br /> <br /> He's fanatically devoted to I'chan, God-Emperor of the Djala. He doesn't wipe out other gods' worship, just forces their priests to accept that I'chan is supreme, and replaces their festivals with festivals devoted to I'chan.<br /> He also forces the Djala to stop referring to Black Spot, traditional Goddess of the Djala, as such. Now they have to accept she's just I'chan's younger sister.<br /> The old high priest wasn't devoted to the new theology enough, after which he &quot;went into seclusion of his own free will&quot; and Fulgens kindly sealed him up &quot;to protect him from distractions&quot;. With no food, as his faith surely would sustain him. It did not.<br /> <br /> The Djala have a big problem with lack of food due to being massively overpopulated, so Fulgens has invaded several nearby areas to take their food and get living space for his people.<br /> <br /> But don't get the wrong idea, Fulgens is no dictator! He's just one member of the Council of Six, along with the new High Priest (who he appointed) and the four directional kings/queens (two of whom gained their position with Fulgens' military help, one hardly ever comes to the council because it's too far away, and one got his position after his father was kidnapped by one of Fulgens' circlemates).<br /> <br /> Fulgens' expansion into nearby areas caused him to clash with the local allies of H'hui'shan, a magical mountain kingdom (run by another PC).<br /> We had a peace conference, and nearly got peace. But the Realm sent a magical message and convinced Fulgens to let them invade and conquer H'hui'shan. Then they could fight each other later. If Fulgens beat the Realm, he'd be able to seize H'hui'shan (which he considers strategically important for the jungle, as it's the source of the great river). We tried to convince him that he should defend H'hui'shan from the Realm... and he decided he'd do so, by conquering it so he could then garrison it, as an alliance would never work due to lack of trust.<br /> <br /> So the war started with some clashes, but as one's a jungle and the other's in the mountains, it's mostly been a proxy war of their &quot;allies&quot; amongst the lake towns.<br /> <br /> The social Lunar of our group eventually convinced him to come help protect the Cult base from Harborhead. He was on the way, when he discovered that the party's Zenith had burnt down a Djala trading post, so he arrested him.<br /> My Night Caste turned up, and demanded to know why the Zenith was in the brig. It turned out that the Djala trading post had been hosting slave traders, and the Zenith had burnt down their shops and freed the slaves. The Night felt slave-trading was hypocritical, as so many Djala have been enslaved (and evil, obviously), but Fulgens explained that some people, like non-Djala, are just natural slaves so it's fine, while Djala are naturally free people so it's wrong to enslave them.<br /> (The slave traders actually weren't Djala, just merchants using the Djala's trading post, but this wasn't explained to my character)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:17:03-07:00","id":1240441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240424#post1240424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly! Bad people defined by their evil deeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that to be a very simplistic assessment of assassins, and the motivation of assassination.<br /> <br /> I may be biased; I come from a country whose liberty was built on a foundation of assassination. I wouldn't exactly call Michael Collins' Twelve Disciples saints, and I certainly wouldn't buy into any national mythology that might lionise them (of which I don't think there's much to go around anyway), but I wouldn't simply write them off, even if I think there's something highly distasteful in having, say, shot an old clerk who was a problem for being able to trace IRA money.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmmm... I mean, with the Great Curse 2nd edition First Age Solars, sure. I don't generally see people saying it about Time of Tumult Solars now, in 3rd edition. Partly because there's hardly any mind-control charms (I think that makes a big difference).</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think you're mixing up some of the things that I'm saying. <br /> <br /> How do I put it...<br /> <br /> I think Solar Genghis Khan makes sense as a character concept, warts and all.<br /> <br /> I need to envision what his First Age incarnation looked like at the time of the Usurpation, that is more sophisticated than just &quot;the same, but slightly more extreme&quot;, &quot;the same, but every now and then he would eat a baby&quot;, or &quot;he was a nice guy, and became Genghis Khan because of the Great Curse&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's really actually a comment that is based on accommodating such conquerors in the baseline of acceptable Solars (as in, acceptable to Sidereals), and thus exploring what the Great Curse corruption does to make them so much of a concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not really related to saying the UCS doesn't choose really bad people (you could argue he's okay choosing bad people because he thinks being Solars might make them better).</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;a really bad person&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> A thought that I've had in the past; Frederick William I of Prussia was a terrible father. He utterly terrorised his son, put him through extreme military training and schooling regimens from a young age, reportedly had him severely punished if he made so much as a slight mistake in drills, and when his son was arrested for trying to run away from that life, had no compunctions against having him executed (only stopped by the demands of the Reichstag), and still went on to have the guy's best friend and fellow attempted escapee executed in front of him.<br /> <br /> He also administered Prussia fairly and well, extended public education, reformed the bureaucracy and the tax code, reclaimed land, encouraged immigration of new farmers, and kept the public finances balanced. He lived and worked frugally, paid his own taxes, and didn't even burn candles longer than was needed. He also strongly advocated for Prussian autonomy within the overall Holy Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> Assess him if he were a Solar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that he'd murder his own brother minutes after exalting in case he talked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how they had different castes, they didn't exactly grow up with an intimate relationship, and he'd hardly be the first Solar that needed to kill to protect themselves when newly Exalted.<br /> <br /> His brother was also hardly a random bystander; he was a soldier of the city authorities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, Havesh did exalt while murdering an old man for money. Not the sort of thing you'd assume the UCS would consider a righteous act.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it adds something (not something good, but points worth considering) how Havesh's motivation to do that was seeing an opportunity to try and escape his life of destitution. That and how the old man fought back reasonably well.<br /> <br /> I guess my point is to say that these characters represent scenarios more complicated than &quot;bad person becomes Solar&quot;, and that the details matter between one example and the next, both in terms of what it says about the character being a valid candidate, and what it says about what they'll go on to do in the world.<br /> <br /> I remember a discussion about the domain of Desus, where people were speculating that it would be some kind of elaborate and depraved pit of iniquity and abuse, and Holden commented upon how absurd that was.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:21:39-07:00","id":1240443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240440#post1240440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fulgens Cruciatus, the Dawn in my group, believes that true morality is the strength to protect your people. If you win, you are good, if you lose, you are evil. Once he decapitated a prisoner I'd just taken then mocked me for not keeping my word (because I'd told the prisoner that if he talked, we wouldn't kill him).<br /> <br /> He's fanatically devoted to I'chan, God-Emperor of the Djala. He doesn't wipe out other gods' worship, just forces their priests to accept that I'chan is supreme, and replaces their festivals with festivals devoted to I'chan.<br /> He also forces the Djala to stop referring to Black Spot, traditional Goddess of the Djala, as such. Now they have to accept she's just I'chan's younger sister.<br /> The old high priest wasn't devoted to the new theology enough, after which he &quot;went into seclusion of his own free will&quot; and Fulgens kindly sealed him up &quot;to protect him from distractions&quot;. With no food, as his faith surely would sustain him. It did not.<br /> <br /> The Djala have a big problem with lack of food due to being massively overpopulated, so Fulgens has invaded several nearby areas to take their food and get living space for his people.<br /> <br /> But don't get the wrong idea, Fulgens is no dictator! He's just one member of the Council of Six, along with the new High Priest (who he appointed) and the four directional kings/queens (two of whom gained their position with Fulgens' military help, one hardly ever comes to the council because it's too far away, and one got his position after his father was kidnapped by one of Fulgens' circlemates).<br /> <br /> Fulgens' expansion into nearby areas caused him to clash with the local allies of H'hui'shan, a magical mountain kingdom (run by another PC).<br /> We had a peace conference, and nearly got peace. But the Realm sent a magical message and convinced Fulgens to let them invade and conquer H'hui'shan. Then they could fight each other later. If Fulgens beat the Realm, he'd be able to seize H'hui'shan (which he considers strategically important for the jungle, as it's the source of the great river). We tried to convince him that he should defend H'hui'shan from the Realm... and he decided he'd do so, by conquering it so he could then garrison it, as an alliance would never work due to lack of trust.<br /> <br /> So the war started with some clashes, but as one's a jungle and the other's in the mountains, it's mostly been a proxy war of their &quot;allies&quot; amongst the lake towns.<br /> <br /> The social Lunar of our group eventually convinced him to come help protect the Cult base from Harborhead. He was on the way, when he discovered that the party's Zenith had burnt down a Djala trading post, so he arrested him.<br /> My Night Caste turned up, and demanded to know why the Zenith was in the brig. It turned out that the Djala trading post had been hosting slave traders, and the Zenith had burnt down their shops and freed the slaves. The Night felt slave-trading was hypocritical, as so many Djala have been enslaved (and evil, obviously), but Fulgens explained that some people, like non-Djala, are just natural slaves so it's fine, while Djala are naturally free people so it's wrong to enslave them.<br /> (The slave traders actually weren't Djala, just merchants using the Djala's trading post, but this wasn't explained to my character)</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that I want to say about this is that it's not a character that I would come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:27:04-07:00","id":1240448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240408#post1240408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we know the gods do choose their exalts this edition. Arguing otherwise is pointless. As for Havesh being a rapist, as I said, this is something that developed after he exalts. Also, he's not a rapist in the sense that most of us think of the term. He disguises himself like wealthy people so well, their wives/lovers don't know it's not the real person, and they willingly have sex with him. Yes, it's still a disgusting thing to do, but it's nothing like what we typically consider rape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to disagree. He's a serial murderer who gets off on living someone else's life. These are not traits that magically develop, these are traits that he always had but didn't have the ability to enact on before. I have no problem with a solar being a rapist or a sociopath. I do have a problem with canon trying to tell me that the UCS actively chose these people. An automatic process at least gives it a degree of separation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:35:59-07:00","id":1240453,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure. Not a character I'd play either (but suitable as an NPC). But he's an interesting character, and one that makes the PCs think about their own morality (and very different to that player's other PCs). To what extent do we compromise our ideals? We really need him to fight the Realm (he has War 5 and every single War charm; the Queen of H'hui'shan has War 3 and no War charms, and she's the best general after him).<br /> How do we deal with a villain who's a Solar, and semi-aligned with the PCs?<br /> I tried to kill him a couple of sessions ago (because, you know, he's a bad person and a threat to H'hui'shan which is run by a friend of my character), and the Twilight was furious, threatening to call a jury of Solars to judge whether I should be punished for trying to murder another Solar (in cold blood, while he was sleeping). Is it wrong to murder (or at least try) another Solar? What if he's a tyrant?<br /> In the end, the Twilight did pull me up before the local court, but it was run by the Queen of H'hui'shan who wasn't keen on the Twilight's suggestion I should serve Fulgens as recompense, so she claimed there wasn't enough evidence, even though the Twilight used Judge's Ear to know I was lying, and the Zenith had evidence it was me. That's pretty dishonest. Is it wrong? Should she have been honest, and handed me over to Fulgens so he could order me to kill her?<br /> Difficult moral issues to consider.<br /> <br /> I enjoy having him in the group, though I think that Queen Enhenduanna's player would enjoy fighting the coming Realm legions more than the Djala.<br /> <br /> I think it's reasonable for the ST to say &quot;I want everyone to play a good person because that'll make the game easier for me&quot;, but I don't think the setting should say &quot;no evil Solars&quot; because that restricts the stories you can tell, if you want to tell them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:49:13-07:00","id":1240462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240453#post1240453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's reasonable for the ST to say &quot;I want everyone to play a good person because that'll make the game easier for me&quot;, but I don't think the setting should say &quot;no evil Solars&quot; because that restricts the stories you can tell, if you want to tell them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I'm not saying that, in fact I'm more than fine with evil solars. What I am saying is that the UCS actively turning his back on solars, when by canon he actively exalted solars like Havash probably thousands of times over, makes it nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:16:50-07:00","id":1240470,"title":"","content":"Okay, I rewrote this answer a couple of times, because it kind of sounds a bit aggressive or attacking you. But I can't really find a way to write it that doesn't come off like that. So please bear that in mind when reading it, sorry. I'm not trying to attack you or score points, just have an interesting discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240441#post1240441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;a really bad person&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is a question that many philosophers and theologians have argued about for thousands of years. What exactly are the worst sins? Today we'd probably say genocide or paedophilia, while in the past many might say treason. Jesus said the only unforgivable sin was to insult the Holy Spirit. Many Islamic theologians say the worst sin is<i> Shirk </i>(ascribing partners to God).<br /> And then of course, there's issues of intent vs effect, but let's use &quot;genocide&quot; as a shorthand for &quot;people who'd like to commit genocide,&quot; since a Solar can probably do what they want without worrying about being thrown in prison by the locals.<br /> <br /> What would you consider the sort of people who'd never get chosen as an Exalt?<br /> <br /> <br /> Every time I (or others) talk about bad people, you point out that their actions make sense from a certain point of view, or aren't as bad as they can be presented. Murderers, rapists, tyrants, kinslayers, etc. And I'm not saying that to criticise you; you're actually quite right.<br /> Maybe assassins could be considered not entirely immoral under some situations. Maybe Havesh's motivation isn't &quot;I love killing people because I get off on cruelty and death&quot;, but &quot;I really want to escape my terrible life which I've been given through now fault of my own, and I'm willing to do whatever it takes to do so.&quot;<br /> <br /> But how many evil people in the world can't be explained this way? How many of the worst people in the world today do evil purely because they love evil, and not because of fear, nationalism, culture, taught entitlement, etc.<br /> (I suppose this is somewhat related to how consequentionalist your morality is, I guess, as you mentioned earlier. Feel free to expand on that.)<br /> <br /> Overall, I think your standards for a Solar who's too evil to be chosen are so low that it doesn't really make any difference to me. The only people you mentioned that you definitely wouldn't imagine being chosen as a Solar are white nationalists, which I wouldn't want to use anyway because it'd be extremely anachronistic (though I suppose I might have a Solar villain from a mutant tribe like the Arzhecki who's massively racist, if I wanted to explore modern evils using a classical fantasy setting. Like how Pratchett uses dwarves and vampires to explore issues of multi-culturalism and immigration. Though thinking about it, since all my players are either English or Welsh, ie people considered White, it might be better to have the villain be a regular human, assuming they're playing regular humans, who hates say Zebra-men or Catpeople or something. Or not. And it might not be a good idea anyway. Something to think about though.)<br /> <br /> I guess you also said, a while back (I hope you don't mind me resurrecting this, but I thought it'd be easier than making you restate it. Tell me if you want to change it)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One is that the criteria for selecting Solars excludes people that would be severely greedy, virulently anti-social, or reactionary in a manner that would persecute the underprivileged </div> </div> </div>Severely greedy seems fine to me in case I want to run a greedy Exalted merchant NPC who contends against the party using bureaucracy. That'd be an interesting villain, I haven't tried that yet*. Plus, it's a common sin of Kings, and being the returning rightful Kings is a theme of Solars, so it seems an appropriate deconstruction (and deconstruction of returning rightful Kings is also a theme of Solars!).<br /> I could definitely see it as an appropriate vice for an otherwise heroic character.<br /> <br /> And, I suppose, a neoliberal capitalist would argue that greed is good, as it motivates people to build wealth (most of my players are socialists or anarchists, so I don't think they'd see it that way. But that's why it'd work well for a villain).<br /> <br /> Virulently anti-social... sounds boring, but I could see maybe a Solar sorcerer in their tower. Probably wouldn't be a very interesting character as they'd spend all their time avoiding people. Which probably means they wouldn't do anything interesting, so that does make sense.<br /> <br /> Reactionary in a manner that persecutes the underprivileged... I don't know, that's actually something incredibly common. Persecutes how much? Because some would argue that everyone who votes Tory is reactionary in a manner that persecutes the underprivileged, but while I did enjoy fighting the Abyssal known as the Iron Lady of Despair (she wields a soulsteel handbag), I'm not sure I'd want to say &quot;no Solar Tories.&quot;<br /> (Although one of my players refuses to play Solars because he believes them to basically all be Tories, on account of being the returning rightful kings with divine right, and so only plays Lunars, except when he played Solar Cao Cao)<br /> <br /> Plus, this applies to many aristocrats to some extent, and I wouldn't want to say &quot;no aristocrats.&quot; Hopefully, by hanging out with other Solars from other classes, they'll later learn to stop being so reactionary.<br /> <br /> *So far I had a Solar assassin; an apostate Cult of the Illuminated Zenith, who wanted to overthrow the Incarnae and free humanity from the gods; a conquering Solar Khan; and a cruel and arrogant Twilight cardinal hunting Yozi-cultists with torture, who also made giant monsters for the Khan's army. But no greedy businessmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-30-2018, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:23:33-07:00","id":1240473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240462#post1240462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I'm not saying that, in fact I'm more than fine with evil solars. What I am saying is that the UCS actively turning his back on solars, when by canon he actively exalted solars like Havash probably thousands of times over, makes it nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he's just not perfect at choosing. And that's why he got so depressed and gave it up.*<br /> (If he was perfect at choosing, he might be like &quot;why are these excellent heroes suddenly acting weird? Is it just the pressure of rule? Or is something weird happening?&quot; But if he chose, say, an awful woman who had great potential to be an amazing hero, and then she continued to be pretty awful, he'd blame himself for making a bad choice.)<br /> <br /> Again, I'd maybe slightly prefer it to be automatic. But I don't think it's terrible. And there's some interesting stories you can do with this method that you couldn't if it was automatic (though some would still work fine if PCs thought he chose, even if he didn't).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Mostly. A few Solars, like Yurgen Kaneko, still exalted. I'm not sure why though. How does him turning his face from Creation and back again, interact with the Jade Prison?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:29:45-07:00","id":1240476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to envision what his First Age incarnation looked like at the time of the Usurpation, that is more sophisticated than just &quot;the same, but slightly more extreme&quot;, &quot;the same, but every now and then he would eat a baby&quot;, or &quot;he was a nice guy, and became Genghis Khan because of the Great Curse&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also want to flag this up, because I think it's really interesting and a good idea (and somewhat independent of the discussion of basic Solar morality before being chosen)... but I'm not really sure what the answer to it is.<br /> Maybe you could start a thread about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:07:15-07:00","id":1240490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240476#post1240476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want to flag this up, because I think it's really interesting and a good idea (and somewhat independent of the discussion of basic Solar morality before being chosen)... but I'm not really sure what the answer to it is.<br /> Maybe you could start a thread about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, my basic answer is simple: that where Solars would independently generally be powerful in a manner that would leave them with fewer incentives to create systems that exploit and ruin people, the Great Curse emphasizes and enhances feelings of powerlessness (something that I've derived from considering several example triggers, which seemed to have a running theme of &quot;something bad happening that I couldn't prevent&quot;).<br /> <br /> I imagine the emotions and mannerisms that arise from Limit Break in the context of the scenarios that actually generate Limit, and in that see the processes by which many Solars are driven to increasingly maniacal and irrational methods to keep everything under control, or wind up in a world that is so vast and complex and ultimately beyond their control (and they're well positioned to know it) that that they're in a constant feedback loop of Limit Break. The catharsis represented by restored Willpower even occasionally meaning that you get Solars conditioned to enjoy how dysfunctional their lives are.<br /> <br /> Sprinkle in some mythic extremes and applications of freaky supernatural power (I had a thought that the origin of the Lookshy superweapon to turn people into crystal was a Solar who ultimately fell upon the remarkably obvious solution to the problem of trying to monitor everything, of turning everybody into crystal so that they would be immobile and unchanging, safe and pristine for eternity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:09:28-07:00","id":1240493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240470#post1240470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Virulently anti-social... sounds boring, but I could see maybe a Solar sorcerer in their tower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that when I say &quot;anti-social&quot;, I'm using it in the same sense as things like ASBOs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:14:10-07:00","id":1240494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240448#post1240448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's a serial murderer who gets off on living someone else's life.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a hired assassin who almost exclusively kills people when paid to, and has resolved to only take hits out on members of the 1%. He's not just living other people's lives, he's living the lives of the people who live at the top of the social ladder, of the type he never could have dreamed of before, that is funded by the kind of exploitation that he used to be subject to, and that he probably feels as though the people who currently occupy it don't deserve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:18:30-07:00","id":1240496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240494#post1240494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's a hired assassin who almost exclusively kills people when paid to, and has resolved to only take hits out on members of the 1%. He's not just living other people's lives, he's living the lives of the people who live at the top of the social ladder, of the type he never could have dreamed of before, that is funded by the kind of exploitation that he used to be subject to, and that he probably feels as though the people who currently occupy it don't deserve.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that doesn't justify his actions. Especially not when he killed an old man to exalt. He's always been coldblooded murderer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:24:01-07:00","id":1240501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240496#post1240496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that doesn't justify his actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you not feel murder can ever be justified?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240496#post1240496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially not when he killed an old man to Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there something particularly special about old men?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:46:03-07:00","id":1240506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240501#post1240501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you not feel murder can ever be justified?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do but this feels like it was just done because he could and for quick cash.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:52:57-07:00","id":1240509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240496#post1240496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that doesn't justify his actions. Especially not when he killed an old man to exalt. He's always been coldblooded murderer.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Exalted are cold blooded murderers. Dace, Ranalea, Jade and Arianna each probably have bigger body counts to their name than Havesh does, and I doubt they lose much sleep about it. At the end of the day, Havesh is a professional assassin who primarily kills people he gets contracted to kill. How different is that from a mercenary like Dace who also gets paid to kill people? Sure being an assassin isn't a &quot;nice&quot; profession, but it's hardly monstrous by the standards of adventure fantasy which is chock full of assassins, mercenaries and hit-men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-30-2018, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:59:52-07:00","id":1240514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240509#post1240509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of Exalted are cold blooded murderers. Dace, Ranalea, Jade and Arianna each probably have bigger body counts to their name than Havesh does, and I doubt they lose much sleep about it. At the end of the day, Havesh is a professional assassin who primarily kills people he gets contracted to kill. How different is that from a mercenary like Dace who also gets paid to kill people? Sure being an assassin isn't a &quot;nice&quot; profession, but it's hardly monstrous by the standards of adventure fantasy which is chock full of assassins, mercenaries and hit-men.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's because I see Dace still doing it as a job rather than Havash who clearly enjoys every step of the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:07:49-07:00","id":1240518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240496#post1240496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially not when he killed an old man to exalt. He's always been coldblooded murderer.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240506#post1240506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do but this feels like it was just done because he could and for quick cash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I'm not necessarily saying that people that have lived their entire lives in the literal gutter should be allowed to get away with murder for the sake of a bit of cash that might improve their lives (or let them have a week or so in which they don't go to bed starving), but I think those circumstances say a bit much about their character.<br /> <br /> There are places in the world where people very much like Havesh have done the kinds of things that he was attempting at the moment that he Exalted at much younger ages. Mind, some of them are doing it specifically because they want to go to prison for a good long time, thinking (not quite inaccurately) that it will be nicer than how they've been living up to that point.<br /> <br /> It's easy for your blood, and many other parts of you, to turn cold when you've never had a house or slept in a bed.<br /> <br /> Havesh enjoyed what he had up until the point that he was forced to go on the run, but more in the manner of sticking it to the elites and finally getting to live the high life, rather than 100% because of sadism (although he is a bit sadistic).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:30:59-07:00","id":1240525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240440#post1240440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fulgens Cruciatus, the Dawn in my group, believes that true morality is the strength to protect your people. If you win, you are good, if you lose, you are evil. Once he decapitated a prisoner I'd just taken then mocked me for not keeping my word (because I'd told the prisoner that if he talked, we wouldn't kill him).<br /> <br /> [...]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of my favorite characters from long ago and not-Exalted was a paladin of a very harsh and draconic religion. The faith had good gods and bad, from a human(oid) perspective. From its own perspective it had a law-of-power + responsibility-of-power sort of ethical stance. <br /> <br /> He was also a dedicated royalist, who believed wholeheartedly that the king or queen of the land was chosen, empowered, and tasked by the dieties to rule. Good or bad. <br /> <br /> One time, when I actually got to play, we encountered an impoverished and haunted land where the living peasants were barely hanging on under brutal rule. The GM had a huge encounter planned out. It turns out that the king of the land was a lich, but the lich was empowered by the legitimate gods of the faith. <br /> <br /> My paladin thought for a moment, bowed, and left. The rest of the party followed, shocked and agape. Good times. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thread content: Past lives seem to be like amnesia. Unless your player gives you leeway to surprise them, it's best to talk out some ideas with them before revealing what evils they'd been up to back then and responsible for now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:48:33-07:00","id":1240530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240473#post1240473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... *Mostly. A few Solars, like Yurgen Kaneko, still exalted. I'm not sure why though. How does him turning his face from Creation and back again, interact with the Jade Prison?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I just can't quit you fuckers...&quot;<br /> <br /> The metaphor that Exaltation in a way is an act of love for the Sun makes sense here. The Jade Prison didn't get everyone and it's notable that Exaltations aren't like, in a hurry to Exalt people every second. Of the probably score or so Exaltations free, he probably only actually Exalted someone once every few years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:51:38-07:00","id":1240531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240514#post1240514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's because I see Dace still doing it as a job rather than Havash who clearly enjoys every step of the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Havesh is a monster, then he was a monster mainly created by his society, and he enjoys bringing retribution down on the heads of the rich and powerful who profit while people like him are forced to sleep in gutters and eat out of trash cans. And that kind of archetype about the poor nobody who is taking retribution out on the wealthy elites who pushed him around is ancient and has appeared in many stories.<br /> <br /> Of course Havesh isn't a nice-guy &quot;Robin Hood&quot; type character. That was intentional, he was one of the Solars expressly written to cleave closely to the tales of the Anathema that the Dragon Blooded tell so he was supposed to fall a bit more towards the villain slot than the typical hero slot. Still, there's quite a bit more to him than just being some kind of two dimensional sadistic serial killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:54:55-07:00","id":1240533,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I don't think &quot;serial killer&quot; is even that accurate a thing to call him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:57:15-07:00","id":1240535,"title":"","content":"You know, I realised that if I was going to look for reference points for Havesh in other fiction, one of the better choices would be just about any major character from the Guardians of the Galaxy movies. Maybe it would help his image a bit if he quipped occasionally, or was portrayed by a charismatic and attractive man. That's not really something that I would want to fault him for, considering that I don't think he's ever had a positive relationship or any kind of reinforcement in his life.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I can't really take the idea that Havesh was intended as a depiction of a Solar that goes down the wrong path and abuses the power bestowed upon him, when he's given the backstory of having been a homeless orphan. That's kind of the worst thing that it's possible to be, consistently at any point throughout human history. Kind of an endless tirade of mind-numbing boredom, deprivation, necessary violence, and if you manage to never actually be abused, it's probably a spectre that you live under constantly. If he was supposed to be straightforwardly bad, he probably should have come from a reasonably comfortable background.<br /> <br /> Certainly, if the development of his empathy was greatly stunted from having probably barely ever experienced it, he's at least doing well enough to direct his ire towards the people that benefit from and perpetuate the social hierarchy that resulted in his entire life up until he was Exalted being a miserable slog, rather than taking their cue and going for the more vulnerable people in his immediate vicinity.<br /> <br /> I often think about how the cruellest murder that Havesh ever committed, the one that entailed a bit of torture and was not prompted by payment or self-preservation, was directed at a man that he had earlier seen go out of his way to abuse a homeless person, because he was so very certain of the rightness of his privileged social station as a result of having been born at a certain time of the day, and because he didn't think that anybody would stop him.<br /> <br /> Havesh might improve a bit if he ever had a friend, preferably one whose draw to him is not predicated on a desire to exploit his talent for murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T13:20:21-07:00","id":1240562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240531#post1240531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Havesh is a monster, then he was a monster mainly created by his society, and he enjoys bringing retribution down on the heads of the rich and powerful who profit while people like him are forced to sleep in gutters and eat out of trash cans. And that kind of archetype about the poor nobody who is taking retribution out on the wealthy elites who pushed him around is ancient and has appeared in many stories.<br /> <br /> Of course Havesh isn't a nice-guy &quot;Robin Hood&quot; type character. That was intentional, he was one of the Solars expressly written to cleave closely to the tales of the Anathema that the Dragon Blooded tell so he was supposed to fall a bit more towards the villain slot than the typical hero slot. Still, there's quite a bit more to him than just being some kind of two dimensional sadistic serial killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than chose to make something better of himself or the city, he did what he always did and took advantage of his powers just to kill people and make money. Havesh had plenty of options and he took the one that was easy and fun for himself. I don't know why you think someone who was poor can't just be a shitty person. I used to live in one of the worst places in miami for 14 years of my life. Shitty people would be shitty regardless of how poor or rich they were. That's just a poorly rationalized excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T13:23:49-07:00","id":1240564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240535#post1240535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I realised that if I was going to look for reference points for Havesh in other fiction, one of the better choices would be just about any major character from the Guardians of the Galaxy movies. Maybe it would help his image a bit if he quipped occasionally, or was portrayed by a charismatic and attractive man. That's not really something that I would want to fault him for, considering that I don't think he's ever had a positive relationship or any kind of reinforcement in his life.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I can't really take the idea that Havesh was intended as a depiction of a Solar that goes down the wrong path and abuses the power bestowed upon him, when he's given the backstory of having been a homeless orphan. That's kind of the worst thing that it's possible to be, consistently at any point throughout human history. Kind of an endless tirade of mind-numbing boredom, deprivation, necessary violence, and if you manage to never actually be abused, it's probably a spectre that you live under constantly. If he was supposed to be straightforwardly bad, he probably should have come from a reasonably comfortable background.<br /> <br /> Certainly, if the development of his empathy was greatly stunted from having probably barely ever experienced it, he's at least doing well enough to direct his ire towards the people that benefit from and perpetuate the social hierarchy that resulted in his entire life up until he was Exalted being a miserable slog, rather than taking their cue and going for the more vulnerable people in his immediate vicinity.<br /> <br /> I often think about how the cruellest murder that Havesh ever committed, the one that entailed a bit of torture and was not prompted by payment or self-preservation, was directed at a man that he had earlier seen go out of his way to abuse a homeless person, because he was so very certain of the rightness of his privileged social station as a result of having been born at a certain time of the day, and because he didn't think that anybody would stop him.<br /> <br /> Havesh might improve a bit if he ever had a friend, preferably one whose draw to him is not predicated on a desire to exploit his talent for murder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Havash bothered me more because he's a rapist then because he's a murderer.Maybe I missed it in this thread, but that's the mark of the wrong path to me. &quot;I murder rich folks and take there stuff&quot; is fine, all things considered. It's not a special kind of bad. Rape is.<br /> I'd be less bothered if Havash living up life as the wealthy didn't include sleeping with his victims wives.<br /> <br /> As for the great curse...I'm fine with cartoonish evil. I'm fine with First Age Solars traping political prisoners in war golems to fight on the fields of battle, of chaining rivers to starve dissedents, of being all varieties of nightmarish awful there ever was. My own games featured First Age Solars that:<br /> -that established an cult of ethnic cleansing and genocide,crafting sorcerous creatures and leading legions in a fascist death cult to establish a perfect order before his Lunar Mate 10 Plauges his empire.<br /> -Preformed invasive alchemical experiments on his martial arts students and himself, eventually creating a being out of his inner id that murdered him<br /> -Built a vast forge that employed demons from malfeas in an effort to make a perfect metal idol to replace the sun, ulimately kidnapping and enslaving dissedents and locking them in suits of iron that forced them to work before Sidearals killed her for attempting to recreate a prehuman race of demon-priests<br /> -Trapped five behemoths in his crown and used their power to puruse a number of failed and bloody wars, before finally seeling them ina vast yasal crystal beneath ysyr<br /> -Trapped an army of fae in bodies of brass to create a legion of djinn and enslave the local population<br /> -Traversed the realms of existence and collected people he liked in his vast manse, before going to the ruin-land of Zen Mu and being devoured by a dragon there.<br /> <br /> My point of reference for the Usurpation, I guess, is mythic extinction events: Floods, wraths of God, sinkings of continents, and so on. Which means evil of a scope, scale, and depth that it's rather ...silly.<br /> My only preference is that it's not 'just' solars who were decadent, catastrophic monsters that really needed to be stopped from their vast and self consuming hubris. At minimum Lunars I prefer to implicate as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:04:51-07:00","id":1240578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240562#post1240562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than chose to make something better of himself or the city, he did what he always did and took advantage of his powers just to kill people and make money.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did he &quot;take advantage of his powers just to kill people and make money&quot; prior to his Exaltation? Because aside from the one time where he Exalted in the act, I don't really see that as something he &quot;always&quot; did. <br /> <br /> The whole point was that prior to his Exaltation, <i>power was not a thing he had</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240562#post1240562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just a poorly rationalized excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better than one more bullshit &quot;picked himself up by his bootstraps&quot; story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-30-2018, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:20:03-07:00","id":1240584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240578#post1240578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did he &quot;take advantage of his powers just to kill people and make money&quot; prior to his Exaltation? Because aside from the one time where he Exalted in the act, I don't really see that as something he &quot;always&quot; did.<br /> <br /> The whole point was that prior to his Exaltation, <i>power was not a thing he had</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need power to kill anyone or hurt people so you can get something you don't own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Better than one more bullshit &quot;picked himself up by his bootstraps&quot; story. </div> </div> </div>You make it sound like people never do that. That still doesn't condone his actions which you seem to have no problem doing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:45:10-07:00","id":1240595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240584#post1240584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need power to kill anyone or hurt people so you can get something you don't own.</div> </div> </div> </div>He certainly didn't imply in the text that he'd ever killed anyone prior to that instant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240584#post1240584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make it sound like people never do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want you to do me a favor.<br /> <br /> If you have a pair of boots, go and put them on. If you don't have a pair of boots, go get a pair, and get back to me. <br /> <br /> Now, try and lift yourself off the Earth completely; free yourself from the tyranny of gravity and surfaces by dint of nothing but your own arm muscles pulling up on your boot-straps.<br /> <br /> <i>Did it work?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-30-2018, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:35:37-07:00","id":1240611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240419#post1240419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We actually asked Eric Minton about this on our latest episode! Give it a listen and see what he says. I personally found it both illuminating and a little frustrating, if I'm honest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Listening to it now. You guys are big laughers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:50:38-07:00","id":1240619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240595#post1240595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He certainly didn't imply in the text that he'd ever killed anyone prior to that instant.<br /> <br /> I want you to do me a favor.<br /> <br /> If you have a pair of boots, go and put them on. If you don't have a pair of boots, go get a pair, and get back to me.<br /> <br /> Now, try and lift yourself off the Earth completely; free yourself from the tyranny of gravity and surfaces by dint of nothing but your own arm muscles pulling up on your boot-straps.<br /> <br /> <i>Did it work?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm done with this because it'll devolve into personal attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:56:39-07:00","id":1240621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240562#post1240562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than chose to make something better of himself or the city, he did what he always did and took advantage of his powers just to kill people and make money. Havesh had plenty of options and he took the one that was easy and fun for himself. I don't know why you think someone who was poor can't just be a shitty person. I used to live in one of the worst places in miami for 14 years of my life. Shitty people would be shitty regardless of how poor or rich they were. That's just a poorly rationalized excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, he Exalted during his first killing. If he went back to what he was doing before he Exalted, he'd go back to starving in the gutter. Besides, like I pointed out earlier, there are lots of Exalted who were assassins or mercenaries who dealt death before they Exalted, and then continue to do so after they Exalted. In his write up Havesh has a keen understanding that so far the Dragon Blooded have killed every Anathema who's appeared throughout history, and if he drew a lot of attention to himself, they'd hunt him down too. So he keeps a low profile and tries not to attract attention because he doesn't want to end up dead.<br /> <br /> Now whether that's a cowardly decision or a pretty wise one depends on perspective.<br /> <br /> As to Havesh being a shitty person, yeah he's a shitty person. So are loads of other Exalted. All that said, I think we've seen some moving of arguments about Havesh over the thread, from the problem that he's a serial killer, to the problem being that he's a cold blooded murder, to just being a shitty person in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:14:58-07:00","id":1240628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240621#post1240621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, he Exalted during his first killing. If he went back to what he was doing before he Exalted, he'd go back to starving in the gutter. Besides, like I pointed out earlier, there are lots of Exalted who were assassins or mercenaries who dealt death before they Exalted, and then continue to do so after they Exalted. In his write up Havesh has a keen understanding that so far the Dragon Blooded have killed every Anathema who's appeared throughout history, and if he drew a lot of attention to himself, they'd hunt him down too. So he keeps a low profile and tries not to attract attention because he doesn't want to end up dead.<br /> <br /> Now whether that's a cowardly decision or a pretty wise one depends on perspective.<br /> <br /> As to Havesh being a shitty person, yeah he's a shitty person. So are loads of other Exalted. All that said, I think we've seen some moving of arguments about Havesh over the thread, from the problem that he's a serial killer, to the problem being that he's a cold blooded murder, to just being a shitty person in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. My point was, I don't think the UCS should have a say in who gets exalted. It just gives this completely different version of what happened in the first age. He turned his back because the the solars were acting like assholes. however, if he's the one who exalted them, that basically means this situation should have been a forgone conclusion. I just don't like the implication. Having them be out of his control at least gives some semblance of rationality to his decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:31:53-07:00","id":1240648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240628#post1240628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. My point was, I don't think the UCS should have a say in who gets exalted. It just gives this completely different version of what happened in the first age. He turned his back because the the solars were acting like assholes. however, if he's the one who exalted them, that basically means this situation should have been a forgone conclusion. I just don't like the implication. Having them be out of his control at least gives some semblance of rationality to his decision.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the Unconquered Sun does his best to Exalt people who are righteous and virtuous (by his own standards) but he's explicitly neither omniscient nor omnipotent, so occasionally he may Exalt someone without having a complete understanding of all of their flaws. He might Exalt someone who is exhibiting great bravery without realizing that they're a horrible monster who enjoys murdering children. That said, the Unconquered Sun is probably a pretty good judge of character, so that likely doesn't happen very often, just often enough that if a Storyteller needs a complete scumbag as a Solar or a player wants such a character for a PC, they have that option.<br /> <br /> Further, I don't really see an issue though with the idea that even the best of people can become corrupt over time, and that even the UCS made sure to undertake the most perfect vetting process he possibly could, over the course of the millennia that the First Age lasted, many of the Exalted became assholes, especially once you factor the Great Curse in. That's not really the Unconquered Sun's fault or something you can lay entirely at his feet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:54:02-07:00","id":1240657,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the ucs is as close to perfect as anyone in the setting can get, innately. I find it impossible to believe he'd make mistakes. He's literally built not to. Either he purposely exalts these people knowing full well their predisposition and what they'll become with that power. Or it's just out of his hands and the exaltations try their best to exalt someone &quot;good&quot; but have nebulious possibly odd criteria. I obviously prefer the latter the second gives way to too many issues in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:01:24-07:00","id":1240661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240657#post1240657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the ucs is as close to perfect as anyone in the setting can get, innately. I find it impossible to believe he'd make mistakes. He's literally built not to. Either he purposely exalts these people knowing full well their predisposition and what they'll become with that power. Or it's just out of his hands and the exaltations try their best to exalt someone &quot;good&quot; but have nebulious possibly odd criteria. I obviously prefer the latter the second gives way to too many issues in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are people who live in their parent's basements playing video games all day and ignoring any semblance of responsibility considered 'perfect' now?<br /> <br /> I think you maybe have read too much about how great TUS is and not enough about how the setting rejects the <i><b>idea</b></i> of perfection time and time again. Malfeas embodied the very concept of rulership. Cecelyne embodied the very concept of Heirarchy. TUS was created to embody the concepts of excellence and virtue.<br /> <br /> NONE OF THEM ARE PERFECT.<br /> <br /> If TUS was anything like how you seem to portray him, then no one would be necessary for anything because TUS would just do everything, perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:12:22-07:00","id":1240664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240657#post1240657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the ucs is as close to perfect as anyone in the setting can get, innately. I find it impossible to believe he'd make mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you say, he's about as close to perfect as anyone in the setting can get, and yet he's made some pretty major mistakes so he's clearly pretty far from being actually &quot;perfect.&quot; Again, he's never been presented as anywhere close to omnipotent or omniscient, even during the height of 2nd edition Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:13:21-07:00","id":1240665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240661#post1240661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are people who live in their parent's basements playing video games all day and ignoring any semblance of responsibility considered 'perfect' now?<br /> <br /> I think you maybe have read too much about how great TUS is and not enough about how the setting rejects the <i><b>idea</b></i> of perfection time and time again. Malfeas embodied the very concept of rulership. Cecelyne embodied the very concept of Heirarchy. TUS was created to embody the concepts of excellence and virtue.<br /> <br /> NONE OF THEM ARE PERFECT.<br /> <br /> If TUS was anything like how you seem to portray him, then no one would be necessary for anything because TUS would just do everything, perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div> The ucs is embodied by the solars who can perfectly measure the worth of a human. It shouldn't be hard for him to do the same thing. I just don't get why the god has to be the one to personally exalt them because it just takes out the mystery of why the exaltation was chosen. I feel it takes away a lot of things and adds nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:14:17-07:00","id":1240666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240664#post1240664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you say, he's about as close to perfect as anyone in the setting can get, and yet he's made some pretty major mistakes so he's clearly pretty far from being actually &amp;quot;perfect.&amp;quot; Again, he's never been presented as anywhere close to omnipotent or omniscient, even during the height of 2nd edition Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he's not omnisecient then how does he pick who exalts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:21:10-07:00","id":1240667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240619#post1240619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm done with this because it'll devolve into personal attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, then why are you still posting in this thread?<br /> <br /> Pulling yourself out of poverty or homelessness or depression by your bootstraps is a futile and foolish gesture; <i>that's why they coined the phrase that way</i>. There is no self-made man, and you should be leery of anyone who tells you different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:22:27-07:00","id":1240668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240667#post1240667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, then why are you still posting in this thread?<br /> <br /> Pulling yourself out of poverty or homelessness or depression by your bootstraps is a futile and foolish gesture; <i>that's why they coined the phrase that way</i>. There is no self-made man, and you should be leery of anyone who tells you different.</div> </div> </div> </div>No i'm done talking to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:08:12-07:00","id":1240680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240666#post1240666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he's not omnisecient then how does he pick who exalts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he has a magical mirror he uses to peek in on Creation and sometimes spots people doing things he finds interesting and bam, they're Exalted. He's clearly not omniscient however. If he were he'd know everything, all about the Great Curse, how it affected the Exalted and how to cure it, and everything else besides. But we've never seen anything in the books remotely hinting at that. Even the Maidens were never hinted at being truly omniscient, only knowing what they could divine in the reflections of Samsara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:21:33-07:00","id":1240684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240680#post1240680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe he has a magical mirror he uses to peek in on Creation and sometimes spots people doing things he finds interesting and bam, they're Exalted. He's clearly not omniscient however. If he were he'd know everything, all about the Great Curse, how it affected the Exalted and how to cure it, and everything else besides. But we've never seen anything in the books remotely hinting at that. Even the Maidens were never hinted at being truly omniscient, only knowing what they could divine in the reflections of Samsara.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just seems to be in favor for it being out of the UCS's control same with luna. The sidereals are destined to exalt so whether the loom or the maidens do it, is almost the same. However, in previous editions even autochthonians and those outside of creation could exalt as solars and lunars. Either the process happens through a means that's omniscient, or every solar that exalted during the night or out of creation is invalid, as well as every lunar who exalted during the day or in areas outside creation and the wyld. Tying the process to the gods just doesn't make sense with the setting, and I still haven't gotten a valid reason, other than canon, as to why it make's sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-30-2018, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:56:48-07:00","id":1240695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240684#post1240684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either the process happens through a means that's omniscient, or every solar that exalted during the night or out of creation is invalid, as well as every lunar who exalted during the day or in areas outside creation and the wyld. Tying the process to the gods just doesn't make sense with the setting, and I still haven't gotten a valid reason, other than canon, as to why it make's sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's stopping the Unconquered Sun from having magic mirror that lets him gaze out onto Creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:02:31-07:00","id":1240699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240695#post1240695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's stopping the Unconquered Sun from having magic mirror that lets him gaze out onto Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that before the usurpation he turned his back on creation and focused 100% on the games. This just seems like a dumb idea to justify a change that was never necessary in the first place. In previous editions, the gods didn't actively control exaltations, which meant they could go anywhere and mostly choose anyone with very specific but vague constraints. Simply because the UCS or luna or the maidens don't choose their exalt still doesn't mean they wouldn't visit them upon exalting or leave messages. The exaltation being tied to a god just add too much baggage to make sense in the setting, unless these beings a wholly all seeing beings who can look at everyone in and out of creation and choose.<br /> <br /> Edit- To just humor the notion. At any given time there are probably 100's of actions which align with solar exaltation every few hours. That would almost certain require a very dedicated process to choose. Even if the mirror choose the &quot;best&quot; at the right time, it's no longer the UCS picking, it's the mirror. At which point, what say does the UCS have in this process. Why even bother with the UCS if the mirror chooses and why does this mirror have to be a physical thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-30-2018, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:14:31-07:00","id":1240702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240699#post1240699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit- To just humor the notion. At any given time there are probably 100's of actions which align with solar exaltation every few hours. That would almost certain require a very dedicated process to choose. Even if the mirror choose the &quot;best&quot; it's no longer the UCS picking, it's the mirror. At which point, what say does the UCS have in this process. Why even bother with the UCS if the mirror chooses and why does this mirror have to be a physical thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the mirror be picking? I'm talking more like he has a magical artifact that lets him peek out into the world. It doesn't pick, he picks. Hell, maybe it even just randomly shows him various places.<br /> <br /> Maybe one day he's peeking down at Nexus where he sees Panther agonizing over his existence and wanting to change things, find himself sympathizing with Panther and then boom, Panther is Exalted. Then he plays the Games of Divinity for a couple of days. Then peeks down at Chiaroscuro but doesn't happen to see anyone that particularly stood out so nobody Exalted. Then maybe the next day he's looking out in the West where he spots Moray Darktide and the grim warrior's battle prowess impresses him and boom, now Darktide is Exalted.<br /> <br /> That's just one possibility. There are tons of other possible ways that the Unconquered Sun might be able to know what's going on in Creation at certain points in time without having to be completely omniscient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:20:54-07:00","id":1240705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240684#post1240684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just seems to be in favor for it being out of the UCS's control same with luna. The sidereals are destined to exalt so whether the loom or the maidens do it, is almost the same. However, in previous editions even autochthonians and those outside of creation could exalt as solars and lunars. Either the process happens through a means that's omniscient, or every solar that exalted during the night or out of creation is invalid, as well as every lunar who exalted during the day or in areas outside creation and the wyld. Tying the process to the gods just doesn't make sense with the setting, and I still haven't gotten a valid reason, other than canon, as to why it make's sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Because it makes perfect sense to me. If I was a god, and had imbued some exaltations with my power. Then the other gods said to me; &quot;hey, lets setup a system to auto-select candidates based on certain criteria&quot;. My response would have been something like; &quot;The hell with that. I only have so many of these, I'm going to choose who gets them myself!&quot; The Incarnae don't follow the same rules as we do. They don't even follow the same rules as the other gods. It's entirely possible that Luna is contemplating her next move in the Games Divinity, observing Creation for potential new Lunar candidates, and shining her light into the wyld as a beacon for Gaia (assuming that story hook is still a thing).<br /> <br /> While the Incarnae may choose potential exalts as they wish, I don't believe they have a morality sensor, or good-guy/gal detector. They choose candidates they see some potential in, and exalt them as they choose. However, they don't have any special incite into the human soul, nor can they see the future (with some caveats for the Maidens of course). I really like that the Incarnae choose their exalts. I also like that, sometimes, those they choose turn into complete ass-hats. It would mean the Incarnae simply don't fully understand the human psyche. This to makes sense to me. How could a god, created at the beginning of time with all the power of one of the Incarnae, ever understand what it means to grow up poor, homeless, starving, and treated like living garbage! TUCS saw Havesh, and saw a cunning young man, who grew up in terrible conditions oppressed by the rich, yet he had the will to fight back. Any human could have pointed out that Havesh had never had a positive moral force in his world, and may be prone to answering violence and oppression with more violence and oppression. However, TUCS lacks that perspective. None of the Incarnae truly understand mortals. This makes their chosen exalts all the varied and interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:07:32-07:00","id":1240711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240702#post1240702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would the mirror be picking? I'm talking more like he has a magical artifact that lets him peek out into the world. It doesn't pick, he picks. Hell, maybe it even just randomly shows him various places.<br /> <br /> Maybe one day he's peeking down at Nexus where he sees Panther agonizing over his existence and wanting to change things, find himself sympathizing with Panther and then boom, Panther is Exalted. Then he plays the Games of Divinity for a couple of days. Then peeks down at Chiaroscuro but doesn't happen to see anyone that particularly stood out so nobody Exalted. Then maybe the next day he's looking out in the West where he spots Moray Darktide and the grim warrior's battle prowess impresses him and boom, now Darktide is Exalted.<br /> <br /> That's just one possibility. There are tons of other possible ways that the Unconquered Sun might be able to know what's going on in Creation at certain points in time without having to be completely omniscient.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would give him way more power over exaltations then he probably should have. Especially when he 100% turned his face from creation after the solars essentially betrayed them. This mirror situation just gives the UCS a mirror that works everywhere in and out of creation and look at everything and then determine who to pick. It's automation in another name. There's no point you can bring up that won't lead me to it should be automatic. So maybe we should just agree to disagree, because I cannot see the UCS at any point during his eternal Games of Divinity game playing where he'd spend time to exalt beings he no longer trusted, given the choice. Especially when he'd only exalt them to die again and again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:42:18-07:00","id":1240715,"title":"","content":"Well, I believe in 3rd edition the Unconquered Sun wasn't playing the Games of Divinity 100% of the time like he did back in 2nd edition and instead was occasionally doing other things, including looking in on Creation. Ultimately I feel that if if you imagine that the setting continues to work like it back in 1st and 2nd edition, you will find a lot of the 3rd edition material to be fairly frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:42:58-07:00","id":1240716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240666#post1240666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he's not omnisecient then how does he pick who exalts?</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to beg teh queestion that there's no gap between human level epistemic capability and omniscience. He's probably perspective enough to just be able to do that as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:44:39-07:00","id":1240718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240716#post1240716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems to beg teh queestion that there's no gap between human level epistemic capability and omniscience. He's probably perspective enough to just be able to do that as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still selective omniscience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:59:37-07:00","id":1240721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240718#post1240718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still selective omniscience.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. You don't just get to be the single person who decides what words mean. &quot;Omniscience&quot; refers to knowing <i>everything</i>, all things, all the time, at all places; it's not something you can do halfway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-31-2018, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T22:00:41-07:00","id":1240722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240718#post1240718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still selective omniscience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I don't see a problem with the On High having something like that when it's related othteir previews or interests. Such limitted omnisicence is around for say, Jupiter and secrest, for instance. The Sun and folks he might find particualrly interesting isn't much a stretch, especially since the Incarna live in a bit of the plot-defined Deus Ex Machina realm of such things.<br /> <br /> This is especially since, in the end, it's people doing acts he finds worthy. What thsoe criteria are, how foten they occur, and what he deems worthy are not known, so how broadly or how many he knows or sees o rmisses is kind of even more flexible there to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T22:04:39-07:00","id":1240723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240722#post1240722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I don't see a problem with the On High having something like that when it's related othteir previews or interests. Such limitted omnisicence is around for say, Jupiter and secrest, for instance. The Sun and folks he might find particualrly interesting isn't much a stretch, especially since the Incarna live in a bit of the plot-defined Deus Ex Machina realm of such things.<br /> <br /> This is especially since, in the end, it's people doing acts he finds worthy. What thsoe criteria are, how foten they occur, and what he deems worthy are not known, so how broadly or how many he knows or sees o rmisses is kind of even more flexible there to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that's still thousands of events per day. Especially, as someone who turned his back on creation, being the major part of the exaltation process seems odd. I still don't see the reason he has to personally exalt someone. Why is it so necessary? What does it add?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T22:13:02-07:00","id":1240724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240723#post1240723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that's still thousands of events per day. Especially, as someone who turned his back on creation, being the major part of the exaltation process seems odd. I still don't see the reason he has to personally exalt someone. Why is it so necessary? What does it add?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not being a complete absentee addict of a ruler does wonders for making one more imposing and numinous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T22:13:45-07:00","id":1240725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240723#post1240723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it add?</div> </div> </div> </div>Validity to the design decision to label them &quot;the Chosen.&quot; More resonance with ancient myths where autonomous drone missiles hadn't yet been invented. The assurance that it matters if the Unconquered Sun has turned his back on the world or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-31-2018, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T00:39:40-07:00","id":1240745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240723#post1240723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it so necessary? What does it add?</div> </div> </div> </div>So your Solar can say, &quot;I was chosen by the Sun.&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead of, &quot;I was chosen by an algorithm.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T00:54:07-07:00","id":1240750,"title":"","content":"The Sun can see people doing stuff in creation because he's not just sat in the Jade Pleasure Dome playing the games.<br /> <br /> He's also sitting right there in the sky looking at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T03:18:33-07:00","id":1240780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240564#post1240564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a special kind of bad. Rape is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, before I address anything else that has come up since I last logged in:<br /> <br /> It's my perspective that this attitude of mythologizing rape <i>contributes</i> to rape culture.<br /> <br /> Rape does not represent a particularly dark stain upon one's soul; it's a particular form of violence (or at least human indignity) that emerges from a particular kind of social iniquity. It is not an indication of innate monsters, but of values empowered and normalised by patriarchy.<br /> <br /> Or, as is probably the case with Havesh (even though I've already said that the text itself has an underlying misogynistic bias), simply having an upbringing in which one is never really properly taught empathy (which I'd still say he's a fairly well-adjusted example of).<br /> <br /> Rape is definitely a crime, and it should definitely be punished effectively and consistently. I find the attitude of it being a special kind of evil to actually undermine that, because I find it to create a prejudice that leads to assumptions that a lot of people accused couldn't possibly be rapists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T03:34:37-07:00","id":1240782,"title":"","content":"Hmm, most of this discussion has just turned into arguing the specifics of Exaltation, not much to deal with there.<br /> <br /> Well then:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240562#post1240562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shitty people would be shitty regardless of how poor or rich they were. That's just a poorly rationalized excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're of the belief that the circumstances of one's upbringing have no effect whatsoever on the development of one's personality? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240628#post1240628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. My point was, I don't think the UCS should have a say in who gets exalted. It just gives this completely different version of what happened in the first age. He turned his back because the the solars were acting like assholes. however, if he's the one who exalted them, that basically means this situation should have been a forgone conclusion. I just don't like the implication. Having them be out of his control at least gives some semblance of rationality to his decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm reading correctly, it seems to me that you're saying that your perspective on the Usurpation was that the Unonquered Sun set the Exaltations in motion with a selection process that was not morally discerning, stopped paying much attention, and then when he realised that most of the Solars had gone bad because the process did not sufficiently exclude bad people, he turned away in shame and disgust.<br /> <br /> I can see why that would be viewed as more consistent, particularly to somebody that would largely discount the significance of the Great Curse in the first place.<br /> <br /> For me, it becomes a matter of exploring ideas on what the corrupted Solars were like that actually <i>does</i> make sense of somebody with the disposition of Havesh being Chosen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240657#post1240657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the ucs is as close to perfect as anyone in the setting can get, innately.</div> </div> </div> </div>This attitude probably doesn't carry forth in this Edition.<br /> <br /> Besides, if he was so perfect, then why would the process of Exaltation be flawed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240665#post1240665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't get why the god has to be the one to personally exalt them because it just takes out the mystery of why the exaltation was chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find being chosen actively and with motive by a powerful intelligence whose reasons that you will probably never know is even more mysterious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T04:08:28-07:00","id":1240793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240745#post1240745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your Solar can say, &amp;quot;I was chosen by the Sun.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Instead of, &amp;quot;I was chosen by an algorithm.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like the end result is the same thing one just has less logistical issues. Especially when he wholesale closed himself and his heart from the world. It gives him way too much control over the process which i feel invalidates a lot of the freedom exalted have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:01:24-07:00","id":1240802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240793#post1240793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one just has less logistical issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the Unconquered Sun having an innate awareness of heroic actions across the world have greater logistical issues than Munaxes containing the echoes of every treacherous whisper in all of the world?<br /> <br /> Which is to say, are there logistical issues at all when talking about numinous supernatural beings?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when he wholesale closed himself and his heart from the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to read that as being the only reason that the Jade Prison was actually functional, even if the Sidereals still needed to put in the actual work of making it and wielding it and ensuring that most of the Essences were free to be scooped up.<br /> <br /> Really, the argument that some Solars continuing to exist invalidates the Sun's hermitage if he's supposed to still be Choosing them doesn't really get me, when no version of the setting has ever said that the very small number of Solars generally managed to accomplish much of anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gives him way too much control over the process which i feel invalidates a lot of the freedom exalted have.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? He still can't take it back, and the setting can only really function on the assumption that he's not going to just come down off his cloud and do things himself, or beat up Exalted that he doesn't like (anymore).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:04:30-07:00","id":1240803,"title":"","content":"As I've mentioned before, (at least I think it was on this thread) the current devs have indicated that the process is somewhere in between the two.<br /> <br /> The unconquered sun chooses exalts in the same way one might choose what flavour ice cream they like. It's not a conscious &quot;I shall exalt that mortal&quot; it's a spur of the moment &quot;ooh, I like that one.&quot; and then boom, they're exalted before he can think it through.<br /> <br /> Meaning it's well within the realm of possibility for him to exalt someone and then go &quot;looking at things logically, I probably shouldn't have done that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perfect temperance can stop you from performing actions that you want to do but probably shouldn't, but exaltation never gets to step 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:20:07-07:00","id":1240810,"title":"","content":"Okay.... I'd like to get this back on track. How do you use/incorporate Solar past lives in your Chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:27:10-07:00","id":1240813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240802#post1240802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the Unconquered Sun having an innate awareness of heroic actions across the world have greater logistical issues than Munaxes containing the echoes of every treacherous whisper in all of the world?<br /> <br /> Which is to say, are there logistical issues at all when talking about numinous supernatural beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is when he already has a lot of purviews. Adding this just for exaltation seems, more than odd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I like to read that as being the only reason that the Jade Prison was actually functional, even if the Sidereals still needed to put in the actual work of making it and wielding it and ensuring that most of the Essences were free to be scooped up.<br /> <br /> Really, the argument that some Solars continuing to exist invalidates the Sun's hermitage if he's supposed to still be Choosing them doesn't really get me, when no version of the setting has ever said that the very small number of Solars generally managed to accomplish much of anything. </div> </div> </div>Unless we are going to have the solars never exalt during the 800+ years the wyld hunt was formed, those solars still exalted on a rapid basis and that kind of invalidates them. It also means that despite supposedly turning his back to the world and it's plight he was still actively looking at creation and exalting these solars. It just makes nonsensical because he hasn't turned his back on creation because he's still exalting these solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How so? He still can't take it back, and the setting can only really function on the assumption that he's not going to just come down off his cloud and do things himself, or beat up Exalted that he doesn't like (anymore). </div> </div> </div>It gives him too much say in the process and Eric Minton has said that it works with him dead. So why does the process need to work with him alive. Either you have to add all these restrictions or extra powers to the unconquered sun or you just make it automatic and it suddenly doesn't have to be a thing that interferes with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:59:51-07:00","id":1240821,"title":"","content":"He's turned his face away, but he can still hear stuff going on in the background and occasionally glances back and exalts a mortal he likes. <br /> <br /> Like, I wouldn't be surprised if the replacement speed of solars dropped during the late first age up until the solars came back.<br /> <br /> But anyway, past lives. <br /> <br /> One idea I had was to treat past lives kinda like lore sometimes?<br /> <br /> Like, if you find yourself in your past self's manse you could, like, introduce facts as you &quot;remembered&quot; what was in there. Or what was supposed to be in there. <br /> <br /> &quot;Hmm, in this next room there should be a very powerful daiklave on a stand&quot;<br /> &quot;You have found the stand.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:11:31-07:00","id":1240822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240813#post1240813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is when he already has a lot of purviews. Adding this just for exaltation seems, more than odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the purviews of the Unconquered Sun?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">those solars still exalted on a rapid basis and that kind of invalidates them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also means that despite supposedly turning his back to the world and it's plight he was still actively looking at creation and exalting these solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could also fill in the blank space with an idea that when you're a god of his scope and power, it's hard to not hear even a little bit of what is going on in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just makes nonsensical because he hasn't turned his back on creation because he's still exalting these solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Converse to my idea that the Jade Prison only works while he rejects the Solars is my notion that the Prison was incapable of holding the Essences down when the Unconquered Sun finally decides that enough is enough. I certainly find it to reconcile the Jade Prison still being a thing in the setting with developer references to the idea that the return of the Solars is owed to the Sun.<br /> <br /> In this model, a small number of them being around is a kind of mild lingering affection (predicated a bit on the fact that, despite the best efforts of the Sidereals, they weren't able to get all of them in time).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gives him too much say in the process</div> </div> </div> </div>What does that have to do with freedom?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why does the process need to work with him alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, from a Doylist perspective, I think the matter of writing it that way is not to address some logical consistency matter (which I think is in many cases one of the least interesting ways to write Exalted, see statements of why Alchemicals can't become akuma), and more because the idea of actually being chosen by a mighty god makes the subject matter more intimate and mythic. I think there was too much cynicism around the Second Edition depiction.<br /> <br /> From a Watsonian perspective, I would see it less in terms of need and more in the idea that while the Sun lives, it's going to be a matter that is on his mind, which he wouldn't be liable to ignore or delegate even if he could. From that perspective, I actually see the difference less in terms of the Exaltations having a switch between manual and automatic, that will be flipped should the Sun not rise, but rather that they're a subject of such importance to him that his will on that subject can live on past the point of his actual death in the legacy of his Exaltations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it suddenly doesn't have to be a thing that interferes with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still doesn't. Really, it only seems to if you insist upon a reading of the Unconquered Sun that excludes the possibility of some kinds of Exalted that you would want being in the setting.<br /> <br /> Quite apart from the question of where in the Third Edition core you're getting this from, or why you would cling to Second Edition points that don't need to apply anymore, you really seem to be going in circles with this. People keep pointing out ways to characterize the Unconquered Sun that enable as diverse an array of Solar character backgrounds as possible, and they're just dismissed, or the talking point shifts. You want, what, an Unconquered Sun that is so righteous and infallible that he would never personally choose anybody that would have negative personal qualities, but you also want him to have allowed an automated process that not only does, but does with such consistency that it caused him to disown the Solars?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:17:40-07:00","id":1240825,"title":"","content":"As cool as the breaking of the jade prison being performed by a golden lance launched from heaven would be, it sort of needs to be the deathlords that did it still so that abyssals and infernals can be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:19:34-07:00","id":1240826,"title":"","content":"I mean at this point we should agree to disagree. I don't think we're going to reach the same conclusion because I inherently dislike the change in 3e and we're never going to agree on this. I feel that the UCS's control over exaltation is poor decision and I don't think that'll ever change that decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:43:38-07:00","id":1240835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240825#post1240825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As cool as the breaking of the jade prison being performed by a golden lance launched from heaven would be</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, that's flashier than I have in mind. I envision it more as a case of the Unconquered Sun deciding that enough is enough, and the Exaltations answer his will and burst forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it sort of needs to be the deathlords that did it still so that abyssals and infernals can be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The people that set up nets to catch the salmon that return for spawning season are not behind the life cycle of salmon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:58:15-07:00","id":1240837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240810#post1240810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay.... I'd like to get this back on track. How do you use/incorporate Solar past lives in your Chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>In prior Chronicles, it's been a quick way to load Celestial characters up with possessions and plot demands. At the time, as I recall, we had to pay for Past Lives as a Merit, along with the Artifact, Manse, and all that stuff. It was also pretty much all Storyteller created prior-lives, rather than collaborative or Player-driven. Finally, it was introduced early in the Chronicle, as a ST-diktat statement of prior fact.<br /> <br /> I think those are all fine, but I'm planning some attempted improvements in the next Chronicle. For anybody who may remember, this is the one I've been writing on for a long time, but keeps being on hold due to players' real-life situation changes and finishing up a current game in another setting. Still making plans!<br /> <br /> <br /> Spoiler just in case any of my players are visiting:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> So, here's how I'm planning to improve over prior iterations:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The characters will enter the story with a bit of missing memory how they got there. My players are OK with amnesia stories - but I do suggest checking with your players. This will let them get their gear, and have enough memory to find their way back to manses and the like.<br /> <br /> The actuality of their past lives won't really be a feature during the Essence 1 stories, except perhaps for a few dreams and memories I can use as foreshadowing pretexts. I want them to develop as characters before I throw past-lives demands on them. <br /> <br /> There will be a few other hints that won't directly point to past or other lives - for instance that their Manses will not be in the condition they remember them, and that in certain places that they visit for the first times, some fraction of people living there spontaneously drop dead.<br /> <br /> My players are also OK with time shenanigans, so during the course of Essence 2 or 3, it will become apparent that their past lives aren't exactly past lives in this Chronicle. They're current lives -- but rewound by several years and re-scattered around Creation.<br /> <br /> This will lead right into the Chronicle's Question. Question is a story writing artifact I've been playing with lately - it's the theme of the story, but arranged so that the players decide what the outcome will be. We discover that the other-lives selves are starting to emerge, each with full agency, showing up wherever they were flung. They'll all show up when rolled-back time catches up to the moment when the TSD (Time Shenanigans Device) exploded while several factions were/will be battling for it. <br /> <br /> Some of the alternate selves were battling for the other side. Some became cruel, even villainous. Some became lovers or alt-allies or alt-enemies. Some lost their fights and went into hiding. In all cases, the alts will be derived from the player-driven character ideas, as a spin on what-could-have-been, but without the ST telling players what their actual characters are like.<br /> <br /> The Question, then is &quot;What would you do differently, if you could see where you're headed and had the power to change it?&quot; Or possibly &quot;How much do your friends influence your life?&quot; <br /> <br /> I have at least one player I can maybe interest in taking a death, to be replaced by their own alternate.</div> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:48:46-07:00","id":1240863,"title":"","content":"Does anybody ever use past life memories in stunting? For instance, using the memory of a prior life inventing a certain battle tactic to stunt performing that manoeuvre (or something superficially similar to it) in the modern day?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:54:49-07:00","id":1240864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240863#post1240863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody ever use past life memories in stunting? For instance, using the memory of a prior life inventing a certain battle tactic to stunt performing that manoeuvre (or something superficially similar to it) in the modern day?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did that a few times back in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:58:16-07:00","id":1240867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240863#post1240863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody ever use past life memories in stunting? For instance, using the memory of a prior life inventing a certain battle tactic to stunt performing that manoeuvre (or something superficially similar to it) in the modern day?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's been pretty common in our prior games, yeah. <br /> <br /> Less so for combat, as I recall, but certainly some for generalship, and quite a lot for investigation, perception, and social actions. Not to mention Lore and Occult, both of which past-lives themes seemed to anchor.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:22:15-07:00","id":1240882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1238822-third-edition-solars-past-lives?p=1240810#post1240810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay.... I'd like to get this back on track. How do you use/incorporate Solar past lives in your Chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had a cycle where a villain from the First Age was trying to exploit the circle's Past Lives creations for his plot--logically, the circle went through a dungeon each to find the treasures before he did (with 2 exceptions). Each player also had a powerful artifact their ancestor made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}